window.TC_PORTRAITS=Object.assign(window.TC_PORTRAITS||{},{"aries-aries-aries":["You are through the door before the host has finished saying come in, coat half off, already asking what needs doing. People meet someone plainly glad to be alive and plainly impatient with anything that stalls: a slow queue, a vague answer, a plan with no first step. There is no second self to find behind the first. What you feel is what you say is what you do, usually in one breath. The anger lasts four minutes, the delight lasts all evening, and you cannot see why anyone would hide either.","Sun, Moon and Rising all stand in Aries, so the chart has one voice and one ruler, Mars. Nothing in you disagrees with anything else, which is the pleasure of it and the problem. The Moon feels, the Sun decides and the Rising moves, and they fit together so cleanly that the feeling is already an action before you have noticed it was a feeling. What is missing is an outside view. No light in the chart has ever said wait, so the pause has to be built by hand: a friend, a night’s sleep, a rule you wrote while calm.","Honesty at speed. You say the true thing while it is still useful, you forgive faster than most people can finish being angry, and you start again after a failure with no visible hangover. Your courage is catching in small rooms. People who were stuck find themselves at the front with a plan, and you are delighted for them.","With nothing in the chart to slow you, the sentence and its consequence arrive on different days. You can say the unfixable thing while your whole body is certain, and be sorry by supper to someone who is still hurting on Thursday. Growth is building a delay on purpose: one night before the email, one question before the decision, one friend who is allowed to say no."],"aries-aries-taurus":["People take the slow walk, the low voice and the settled chair as the whole of you, and they plan around a patient person. It is a fair guess and mostly wrong. Behind that unhurried arrival sit an Aries Sun and an Aries Moon that want to go now, say it plainly and be finished by supper. The calm is real, but it is how you enter, not what you are. Anger flares fast and clears faster, and anyone who mistook your quiet for consent finds out in one sentence.","Sun and Moon share Aries, so what you are and what you need speak the same fast language, and Mars rules both. Taurus Rising stands one sign away from each and sees neither well. Venus rules it, it wants comfort and a steady pace, and it cannot quite follow what the fire is doing. That gap is the odd sweetness of this chart. The front slows everything down just enough to be pleasant, and the inside keeps the speed. When all three cooperate you start like a sprinter and finish like a farmer.","Momentum with manners. You start things quickly, and your steady presence keeps people from running for cover, so projects survive your enthusiasm. You are honest without being harsh, hard to rattle in a crisis, and you hold a course long after the first excitement has gone.","The calm can go on too long before the fire is let out, and you may swallow the first flash because it seems rude, then release it sideways. People who read you as patient get ambushed by a sudden verdict. Growth is saying the quick true thing early and gently, so the stillness never has to be a lid."],"aries-aries-gemini":["It is three in the afternoon, the meeting has reached its fourth item, and you have been finished since ten past two. People meet a quick, funny, expressive face with restless hands, and they take you for a talker who is still working things out. The truth is plainer. The Aries Sun and Moon already know what they want, and the Gemini surface is narrating it as fast as it can. You are not thinking out loud so much as running to catch up with a decision.","Sun and Moon both stand in Aries, so will and need speak one fast language, and Mars rules them together. Gemini Rising sextiles both, an easy and friendly angle, and Mercury rules it, so what you feel gets a voice almost the moment it arrives. This is a chart with very little drag. You say what you want and you often say it while doing it. The difficulty is that nothing in you has a brake. Mercury only makes the acceleration eloquent.","Speed that explains itself. You decide fast, say what you mean, and bring people along with your wit instead of leaving them behind. You recover from setbacks in an afternoon, you are good in a crisis, and your plain, quick honesty clears a room of fog.","With no brake in the chart, the sentence and the regret can arrive in the same hour, and the Gemini charm makes the apology sound better than the remark deserved. You may talk past a feeling that wanted one quiet minute. Growth is a pause on purpose: say less than you know, and leave a gap for the answer."],"aries-aries-cancer":["When you are cornered, tired or delighted, you do the same thing: you move fast, and then you feed someone. The Aries Sun and Aries Moon go straight at what they want, with a bluntness you mean no harm by. The Cancer Rising is what people meet first, and it is soft: a warm face, a protective stance, a sense that you are about to offer a chair. Then the ram appears and half the room flinches. They are always surprised that the apology is a casserole.","Sun and Moon share Aries, so what you are and what you need run on one fast engine, and Mars rules both. Cancer Rising squares each of them, a hard angle that sets the soft front against the fast core. Cancer is ruled by the Moon, which gives the shell a pull of its own. All three lights are cardinal, so each wants to start and lead. The friction is constant: you charge, you retreat, and you charge again from the shell.","Courage with a heart. You protect the people you love with real force and real tenderness, and you move first when others hesitate. Your anger clears quickly and your generosity does not, and people feel looked after by someone who would also defend them.","The Cancer front takes offence silently and the Aries core answers loudly, so a small hurt can become a large scene. You may snap, then feed the person you snapped at, and call that an apology. Growth is naming the hurt while it is still small, before either side has to act."],"aries-aries-leo":["One fire wants to be through the door already. A second, the same fire, wants it faster. The third wants to be looked at while it happens. People meet the Leo Rising first: warm, upright, an arrival that makes the room look up. Behind it, the Aries Sun and Moon are simpler and quicker than the presentation suggests. They say what they want, feel it all the way, and have usually moved on by the time you finish being admired for it.","Sun and Moon share Aries, so need and will speak one fast language under Mars, and Leo Rising trines both. Three fire lights, and every angle between them is easy. The Sun rules Leo, so even your Rising answers to your own Sun, and the whole chart moves as one body. Nothing in it resists. That is the pleasure of it, and the problem: no light is placed to say wait, and no light stands outside the blaze to see how it looks.","Radiance with nerve. You walk in, decide, and carry people with you. Your warmth is immediate and your courage is cheerful, and you recover from a setback with no visible hangover. People who were hesitating find themselves at the front of the line, grateful.","Everything in you says go, so a bad idea arrives with full confidence and an audience. You can burn through a friendship the way you burn through an afternoon. Growth is building one delay on purpose: a night, a walk, a second opinion from someone who does not clap."],"aries-aries-virgo":["Watch you at the end of a job. The Aries Sun and Moon have done the loud part, the pushing and deciding, and now you are straightening the bench, naming the jars and putting the hammer back in its own outline. People meet the Virgo Rising: neat, observant, modest, someone who notices what is out of place before saying hello. They are surprised when the fire comes. You are tidy because you are fast, and you need somewhere to put the speed.","Sun and Moon share Aries, so what you are and what you need speak one quick language under Mars, and Virgo Rising stands a quincunx from both: five signs away, with nothing in common. Mercury rules the Rising, so it watches, catalogues and corrects, while the fire acts. The two never quite understand each other. Most of your life is the fire discovering the value of preparation, and the Rising discovering that the work will not finish itself.","Speed with standards. You start fast and finish carefully, which is rarer than either alone. You spot the mistake as it happens and fix it without a speech, you say what you mean in few words, and people trust you with the job nobody else wants to do properly.","Both fire lights agree, and the Virgo front audits what they do, so the critic arrives after every decision. You can act with total confidence and then spend the evening listing what you would change. Growth is letting one thing stand imperfect, and walking away from it while it is still warm."],"aries-aries-libra":["People take you for the peacemaker, and the Libra Rising invites it: easy smile, good manners, a knack for making each person feel considered. They are wrong about the rest. Underneath, the Aries Sun and Moon are two matches in one box, quick to want, quick to flare, quick to clear. You are gracious because you hate an unfair fight, not because you avoid one. When you finally say no, the cold morning air comes in with it.","Sun and Moon share Aries, so what you are and what you need speak one fast language under Mars, and neither argues with the other. The Libra Rising stands opposite both, which puts the whole seesaw on one pivot: charm in front, fire behind. Other people tend to hold the qualities you keep half-hidden, such as patience, tact and the pause before answering, and you meet your own balance through them.","Courage that is easy to be around. You say hard things in a tone people can hear, start before you are sure and apologise gracefully if you were wrong, and read a room fast enough to lead it. You share credit freely, forgive quickly, and make a fight feel fair.","Both lights have one speed, and the Libra front hides it until pressure breaks the manners. You may swallow three small irritations in a row, then answer the fourth like a slammed door. Wanting balance, you can hand decisions to whoever is nearest. Growth is naming the first irritation in the first minute, while your voice is still kind."],"aries-aries-scorpio":["Three in the morning is the hour you know best. The house is quiet, the Aries Sun and Moon have run out of things to do for once, and the Scorpio Rising turns its steady gaze on whatever is left: a conversation, a debt, an old slight. By daylight you look calm, even still, and people sense a depth they cannot name. The spearpoint is out of sight. It has not gone anywhere.","Mars rules the Aries Sun and Moon and, in the older reckoning, the Scorpio Rising too, so all three lights share a planet and a single hunger. Sun and Moon stand together in a doubled sign, with no friction between them, while the Rising is a quincunx from both: what you show in stillness is another register from what you do and what you feel. The fire runs in the open and the depth runs through the walls.","Courage that watches first. You are ready to act and ready to wait, which makes you hard to surprise and hard to move. You notice motive, hold a confidence and strike once, accurately. People feel safer when you are awake.","Three lights ruled by one planet agree about everything, including grudges. The fast fire flares and clears, but the Scorpio Rising keeps the record. You may play down a fury until it has become a settled plan. Growth is saying “that hurt” on the same day, loudly if need be, before the night shift begins."],"aries-aries-sagittarius":["When you are cornered, you run at the wall. When you are tired, you run faster, and when you are delighted you run at the nearest friend to tell them. That is the whole system. People meet the Sagittarius Rising, open, bright and laughing, arriving with news, and they feel invited to widen their lives. The Aries Sun and Moon behind it do the work: wanting, deciding, flaring, clearing. There is a war drum in the chest and a horizon in the eye.","All three lights are fire. Sun and Moon share Aries, so what you are and what you need speak one fast language under Mars, and both trine the Sagittarius Rising, so how you seem and how you feel are never at odds. Jupiter rules the Rising and makes the whole chart larger than it needs to be. Nothing in it supplies a brake or a second opinion.","Courage you can catch. You begin, you invite, you laugh, and other people find they are braver around you. You recover from a setback within the hour, forgive at the same speed, and tell the story so well that the setback becomes the best part.","With no air, earth or water to cool it, the fire has nothing to argue with. You may promise something at full volume and forget it by Thursday, burn a friendship by being honest too fast, or run through three plans before lunch. Growth is one decision made slowly, and one apology made without a story."],"aries-aries-capricorn":["Three voices live in your house. The Aries Sun wants to sprint, in the cold morning air, right now. The Aries Moon agrees and also wants to shout about it. The Capricorn Rising is the foreman at the door with a clipboard, saying the work starts at seven and the wall will still be there tomorrow. People mostly meet the foreman: composed, serious, a little dry, with a handshake that means it. The two fires wait behind him, held sprint and all, until the whistle.","Sun and Moon share Aries, so what you are and what you need speak one fast language under Mars, and both stand in square to the Capricorn Rising, cardinal against cardinal, so front and fire argue over who is leading. Saturn rules the Rising and slows whatever Mars started. Amplified passion, confidence and drive, governed by a patient, serious face.","Drive with discipline. You start fast, finish properly and keep your word. You make a plan and then outwork it, and you can hold back your temper when it would cost you. People trust you with real responsibility, and are surprised by how warm you are once the day is over.","Two fire lights and one earth brake in a hard square, so the engine runs against the handbrake. You may be calm at work and explosive at home, or the other way round. The Capricorn Rising treats anger as unprofessional, so it leaks. Growth is letting the fire speak at a small volume every day."],"aries-aries-aquarius":["You are seen in a doorway, one hand on the frame, a half-built thing in the other, saying let’s just try it. You say it to the engineer, the host and the committee. The Aquarius Rising makes you look cool, curious and a little ahead of the moment, friendly from a distance. The two Aries lights behind it are the flint and the spark: what you want arrives instantly, and so does what you feel. The ram on the high ledge is already looking at the next ledge.","Sun and Moon share Aries, so what you are and what you need speak one fast language under Mars, and both sextile the Aquarius Rising, fire and air, so how you seem cooperates with what drives you when you use it. Saturn and Uranus rule the Rising, structure and surprise. It is a glass house of a chart: very open, very bright, and the fire is visible from outside.","Invention at speed. You try things, drop what fails and keep what works, and nobody makes you feel foolish for the attempt. You are friendly, original and brave, you start what others only describe, and you make a strange idea feel like a safe bet.","Both fire lights run at one speed, and the cool Rising hides it until the experiment catches fire. You may leave the lab with the tests half finished and the credit given away. Anger flares and clears, and the people nearby carry the soot. Growth is finishing one experiment and writing down what you learned."],"aries-aries-pisces":["People take you for the gentle one: soft-focus, receptive, a little faraway, easily led. They imagine someone who goes where the water goes. They have not seen the forge. Behind the Pisces Rising the Aries Sun and Moon are one fast fire, quick to want and quick to flare, and when something matters the mist clears and the war drum starts. You are a ferryman who also runs a forge, and you let people think the river is the whole story.","Sun and Moon share Aries, so what you are and what you need speak one fast language under Mars, and both stand a semi-sextile from the Pisces Rising, a neighbouring sign with nothing in common, a blind spot on each side. Jupiter and Neptune rule the Rising. So the fire cannot quite see the mist, the mist cannot quite see the fire, and other people keep seeing only one of them.","Gentleness with force. You are approachable, kind and open, and you can also act, decisively and at once, when it counts. You protect what you love, recover quickly and forgive quickly. Underestimated at the start, you are very rarely underestimated twice.","Two lights that cannot see the Rising, and a Rising that cannot see them. You may let people mistake you for pliant and then resent the misreading. The fire flares in a fog of its own making. Growth is saying the firm thing early, in the soft voice, so that it is believed."],"aries-taurus-aries":["You are the quickest to start and the hardest to move. Both are true, and the second surprises people more. They meet the Aries arrival: a quick handshake, a decision made, a hand already reaching for the next thing. Then they try to talk you out of your usual chair, your usual order, your particular way of folding towels, and they find a wall of warm, immovable calm. You rush toward what you want and then settle into it for years. The sprint is only how you reach the place you plan to stay.","Your Taurus Moon is exalted, an honoured guest, but it sits one sign from the Aries Sun and Rising, and neighbours like that barely see each other. Mars rules the two lights that move. Venus rules the one that wants lunch. The Aries pair decide and go, while the Moon asks where the food is, whether the bed is made, and why everyone is in such a hurry. It is slow to anger and slower to forgive, and when the grievance finally surfaces the Aries lights supply the volume. You are at peace on days with one fast hour and one long meal.","Follow-through. You can start something in an afternoon and still be tending it ten years on, which almost no one can. Your energy has a body in it: you cook, build, plant and repair, and you make courage feel steady rather than frantic. People trust a decision you made quickly and are still defending without any sign of tiring.","The speed can hide a stubbornness you would never admit to. You commit fast, then defend the choice because it is yours, and a grievance can keep quietly for years behind a cheerful face. You can also run past your own hunger and tiredness until the body calls the debt in. Growth is letting the Moon set the pace of the second half, and changing your mind without calling it defeat."],"aries-taurus-taurus":["The feeling arrives in the body before it has a name. Your shoulders drop, your weight settles into your heels, your hands go very quiet. People read the stillness as nothing happening, and that is their mistake, because the Aries Sun has already made the call and the Taurus Moon is simply refusing to be hurried out of it. You sit down as though the chair were yours, and you say the thing once, pleasantly, in a voice that does not offer to repeat itself.","Moon and Rising share Taurus, so what you feel and how you appear are the same slow animal, and Venus rules both. The Aries Sun stands one sign away from each and is the only light in the chart that wants speed. It decides quickly and then has to wait for two lights that need to be comfortable before they move. Most of your life is the Sun learning that patience is not defeat. Once all three agree, almost nothing shifts you.","Staying power with a pulse. You begin what most people only plan, and you keep going when others reach for the exit. Your steadiness calms rooms, your appetite for good things is infectious, and you can be gentle and immovable in the same sentence.","Two fixed lights can turn a decision into a monument. You may dig in against a change you have not examined, and call the stubbornness loyalty. Comfort becomes the thing you protect instead of the thing you enjoy. Growth is letting the Sun ask the question again, once, before the stone sets."],"aries-taurus-gemini":["Picture a loom: the long strings held taut and steady, the shuttle flying through them from one side to the other. The warp is your Taurus Moon, which wants safety you can touch, good food and a body at ease. The shuttle is everything else, the Aries Sun’s push and the Gemini Rising’s wit, quick, curious and always crossing from one thing to the next. People meet the shuttle. The cloth that results, patient and well made, comes from the frame they cannot see.","Aries, Taurus and Gemini run in a row, so every light has a neighbour, and the Moon is exalted in Taurus, an honoured guest in the chart. The Moon sits a small step from your Sun, a semi-sextile with a slight blind spot. Gemini Rising sextiles the Sun, which gives the fire a clever way to introduce itself. The effect is a chart that is hard to hurry and easy to talk to, quick in manner and slow to change its mind.","Quick hands, steady heart. You can talk, learn and begin at speed, and then keep to what you have begun. People rely on you because you are good company and also dependable. You bring comfort to a plan, and you make ideas feel like something you could live in.","The Taurus Moon digs in where the Gemini surface suggests flexibility, and people take your cheerful manner as agreement. A change you did not choose can sit in the body for days before you say a word about it. Growth is saying “no, not like that” while the sentence is still easy to say."],"aries-taurus-cancer":["Is there enough, and will it still be here tomorrow? The question sits behind almost everything you do. It makes you generous with food and wary of change, and it gives you a firm, quiet hold on what is yours. People meet the Cancer Rising: soft, watchful, quick to offer a chair. The Aries Sun is the nerve that goes out and gets the fruit, and the Taurus Moon is the wall around the orchard that keeps it there.","Your Moon is exalted in Taurus, so need is clear and well supported, though it sits only a step from the Aries Sun and sees it dimly. The Cancer Rising squares the Sun, so the soft front and the bold will keep rubbing, but it sextiles the Moon, which helps: the shell and the comfort-seeking Moon agree about home. Between them, the Sun is outvoted by two lights that want to stay.","Provision with courage. You build things that last, feed people well, and hold your ground gently. When you commit you stay, and when you act you do it with enough force to get the job done. Others feel safe inside the walls you build.","Safety can become the only value. The Taurus Moon digs in, the Cancer front guards, and the Aries Sun is left pacing inside a very comfortable cell. You may refuse a change you have not examined and call it prudence. Growth is opening the gate on purpose, once a season, to see what walks in."],"aries-taurus-leo":["At twenty you think they are opposites: the generous one who lights the room, and the one who will not leave the good chair. People meet the Leo Rising, a warm, upright presence with an easy laugh and a sense of occasion. The Aries Sun is the one who gets up and does something about it. The Taurus Moon is the one who wants the meal to be perfect and the evening to be long. You will learn that taste and generosity are the same gift.","Your Moon is exalted in Taurus, so need is clear, sensual and well supported. It squares Leo Rising, two fixed signs each certain of what it prefers: the Rising wants the show and the Moon wants the table. The Aries Sun trines the Rising and sits only a step from the Moon, a blind spot, so the fire helps the front and hardly hears the Moon. The Sun rules Leo, so the Rising follows the Sun even when the Moon digs in.","Warm, loyal, tasteful abundance. You make good things happen and make them last, you are generous in a way people remember, and you bring real appetite to everything you love. Your calm and your fire both turn up when needed.","Two fixed lights can turn a preference into a monument. You may refuse a change because it would spoil the evening, and call the refusal dignity. Pride and comfort cover for each other. Growth is letting the Sun ask the question again, once, before the evening is set in stone."],"aries-taurus-virgo":["It is a true contradiction and it hides well. You are impulsive and methodical, bold and thrifty, ready to jump and unwilling to buy the wrong jar. People meet the Virgo Rising, someone neat, observant and helpful, and they take you for a careful soul. They are right. They have not met the Aries Sun, who made the decision before the second sentence, or the Taurus Moon, who wants the new thing to be solid, tasteful and made to last.","The Moon is exalted in Taurus, so need is clear and well supported, and it trines Virgo Rising, both earth, so the surface and the interior agree about craft and good materials. The Aries Sun stands a quincunx from the Rising and a small step from the Moon, a blind spot: it hardly sees either. The result is a calm, practical pair doing the work of a fire that wants to leave.","Courage with craft. You begin things, and the Taurus Moon and Virgo Rising see them through. Your taste is good, your work lasts, and people rely on you because you finish. You can hold a standard and a pace at the same time.","Two earth lights outvote the Sun, so a bold impulse is often delayed until it is safe, then resented. You may criticise yourself for a risk and criticise others for not taking it. Growth is trusting the first decision once, and not rebuilding it before supper."],"aries-taurus-libra":["The feeling lands in the throat and shoulders first. You can stand at a gathering looking entirely at ease while your neck tightens, or feel your weight settle into both feet when a plan finally seems solid. People meet the Libra Rising, charming and well turned out, and they relax. The Taurus Moon is the old oak table beneath it, slow, sensual, unwilling to be hurried. The Aries Sun is the sprinter held at the line, waiting for the music to be right.","Venus rules both Moon and Rising, so taste, comfort and pleasant company are the shared language, even though Taurus and Libra stand five signs apart, a quincunx with nothing in common but the planet. The Moon is exalted, so need is steady and trustworthy. The Sun is opposite the Rising and a neighbour to the Moon, a semi-sextile with a blind spot, and keeps being asked to wait for beauty.","Courage with taste. You begin things boldly and make them pleasant to be inside. People feel safe near you and slightly more alive. You are loyal, sensual, practical and graceful at once, and you can make a decision and an evening feel equally well made.","The Taurus Moon digs in, the Libra Rising keeps the peace, and the Aries Sun is left pacing. You may stay too long in a comfortable arrangement and then leave all at once. Pleasantness can stand in for honesty. Growth is saying “I want something different” while the table is still warm."],"aries-taurus-scorpio":["Picture a bell in a valley with a cloth wound round the clapper. Most days it hangs there, heavy and unbothered. When someone pulls the rope hard enough, the sound goes up every hillside at once. That is how you react. The Scorpio Rising is the cloth, charged, still, unreadable. The Taurus Moon is the bronze, slow to heat and slower to forget. The Aries Sun is the hand on the rope, rarely used and very strong.","Taurus and Scorpio face each other across the wheel, so Moon and Rising make a seesaw of possession and surrender, comfort and intensity. The Moon is exalted, so need is clear and steady. Mars rules the Sun and, in the older reckoning, the Rising, so front and fire speak one urge, while the Sun is a semi-sextile from the Moon, a neighbour with a blind spot.","Strength that keeps. Your loyalty is slow to give and does not wear out, your senses are reliable and your nerve is real. You can bear pressure for a long time and then act decisively. People learn that you hold on, and that you hold steady.","Moon and Rising oppose, so you grip. Possessiveness sits beside a distrust of being known, and the Aries Sun is the one that lets go all at once. You may keep quiet about a hurt until the cloth tears. Growth is a smaller, earlier ring: a plain sentence on an ordinary Tuesday."],"aries-taurus-sagittarius":["Can I leave and still have somewhere to come back to? That is the question under most of your plans, and you ask it in the car, in the shower, and at the door with your bag half packed. People meet the Sagittarius Rising: open, laughing, full of news. The Taurus Moon is the old oak table you will want at the end of every trip. The Aries Sun is the red thread that gets pulled first.","The Sun trines the Rising, so how you seem and who you are agree, and the Taurus Moon is exalted, so need is steady. But Taurus and Sagittarius stand five signs apart, a quincunx with nothing in common, so the part that wants a settled home and the part that wants the open road have never been properly introduced. The Sun is a neighbour of the Moon, a semi-sextile with a blind spot.","Adventure with a base. You start journeys, and you know how to make a place feel like home within an hour of arriving. You are generous with food, time and stories, your courage is practical, and you bring back something from every trip that others can use.","The Moon wants to stay, the Rising wants to go, and the Aries Sun leaves first and regrets it at the border. You may stay in a place a year too long and leave a person in a day. Growth is naming which one you want this month, aloud, before the bag is packed."],"aries-taurus-capricorn":["At fifty you will understand that the foundation nobody sees was the point. In your twenties the Aries Sun wanted the sprint and the applause, while the Taurus Moon and Capricorn Rising kept saying, in a patient voice you found irritating, that it should be built to last. You will look at the old oak table, the paid-off debts and the friendships that took years, and see that the slow things were the fast ones in disguise.","Two earth lights and one fire. The Taurus Moon is exalted, so need is steady, and it trines the Capricorn Rising, so feeling and manner agree about quality and time. The Aries Sun squares the Rising, cardinal against cardinal, and is a semi-sextile from the Moon, a neighbour with a blind spot. The fire is the odd one out, and the two earth lights keep gently outvoting it. Bold outside, patient beneath.","Courage that lasts. You begin boldly and make what you begin solid, so your work, your word and your friendships age well. You are sensual, loyal and practical, with an appetite for quality, and you can wait without resentment when waiting is wise.","The Sun wants it now and the earth lights want it right, so you may feel permanently late and permanently rushed. You can dig in behind duty and call it stubbornness. Pleasure gets scheduled. Growth is spending something beautiful without a reason, once a month."],"aries-taurus-aquarius":["You are the most conventional rebel and the most rebellious homebody, and both are sincere. The Aquarius Rising looks cool, original, a little ahead of its time, the one who will tell you about the satellite passing overhead. The Taurus Moon wants the same chair, the same soup, the same morning. The Aries Sun is the ram on the high ledge, standing exactly between them. You weave the future out of very old, very comfortable thread.","The Taurus Moon is exalted, so need is steady, and it squares the Aquarius Rising, fixed against fixed: comfort and novelty both refuse to give way. The Sun sextiles the Rising, cooperation that works when it is used, and is a semi-sextile from the Moon, a neighbour with a blind spot. Bold outside, patient and cautious underneath, and rarely easy on yourself.","Change that holds. You start new things and make them solid, so your ideas get built and last. You are sensual and original, loyal and free, and you bring the future to the table without spilling it. People trust your novelty because it comes with a foundation.","Two fixed lights in a square dig in on opposite sides. You may defend an old habit with a new argument and an old argument with a new habit. The Aries Sun is the one that breaks the deadlock, suddenly. Growth is changing one small thing a month, and keeping the chair."],"aries-taurus-pisces":["The feeling sinks into the belly and the hands, and you settle into your chair to carry it, the way an old oak table settles into a floor. People meet the Pisces Rising: soft, receptive, a little faraway. The Taurus Moon is the oak under it, slow and sensory, wanting warmth, food and a hand to hold. The Aries Sun is the war drum far down, which you hear in the body before you hear it in your head. A sea wind has been on the wood for years.","Three neighbouring signs, Pisces, Aries and Taurus, run in a row, so Sun and Rising make a semi-sextile, Sun and Moon make another, and each of the three barely sees the next. The Taurus Moon is exalted, so need is steady and clear, and it sextiles the Pisces Rising, earth and water supporting one another, so interior and front are friends. Bold outside, patient and cautious underneath.","Tenderness with ballast. You feel deeply and stay solid, you are generous, sensual and patient with people, and you act when it is time. Your calm is real and your warmth is physical. Others rest near you the way they rest near a fire.","Moon and Rising are so comfortable together that the Aries Sun is left out in the weather. You may stay in a soft arrangement for years and then leave in a day. Indulgence quietly stands in for decision. Growth is acting a week before you feel ready, with the oak at your back."],"aries-gemini-aries":["People think the bluntness is a temper and the topic changes are a short attention span. Both are wrong. The bluntness is speed: you say the sentence before you have dressed it. The topic changes are several conversations running at once, and you are following all of them and will come back to the first. You think by talking, and best by talking to someone who talks back. Left alone with a slow afternoon you do not rest. You invent an errand, an argument or a better route home.","Your Gemini Moon sits a sextile from the Aries Sun and Rising, air feeding fire, so the three lights cooperate whenever they are asked. Mars supplies the nerve and Mercury the words, and between them you can start something and explain it while it happens. The Moon’s need is not calm but company: a mind to bounce against, a new subject, a reason to say it aloud. The Aries pair deliver the verdict, and the Moon happily argues the other side to prove it can. Feelings get named fast here, sometimes before they have finished arriving.","Quick mind, quick hands. You can learn a skill at the weekend, pitch it on Monday and make the room laugh while you do. You say what other people are circling, in words they can repeat, and you make bold moves feel like a joke everyone is allowed to join. Few people open a conversation as fast and as truthfully as you do.","With a mind this fast and a will this fast, a great deal gets begun and little gets finished. You can start a project, a quarrel and a friendship in one week and tend none of them, and talk about a feeling so well that you never sit in it. Growth is staying with one thread past the point where the next idea arrives, and learning that silence is not an emergency."],"aries-gemini-taurus":["The hour after a good lunch is when you are most yourself. Your body would like to sit, your Taurus presence has already arranged the cushions, and your mind has left for a different conversation, then two more. People see someone relaxed and chatty. You are actually collecting things: a question to ask, a plan to start, a joke you will use at six. The Aries Sun keeps the whole thing from drifting, because under the easy talk you have a direction and you are going there.","Aries, Taurus and Gemini run in a row, so each light is next to another and none has a long argument with the rest. The Gemini Moon sextiles your Sun, a friendly angle that lends the fire wit and variety. Taurus Rising, ruled by Venus, is the slow ground under the kite string: it keeps you looking unhurried while the Moon is quick and the Sun is quicker. The risk is mostly in the pace, because three neighbours can crowd the day.","Charm that does things. You can explain, persuade, start and finish, and you do it while keeping the room comfortable. People relax around your voice, then discover you have been steering. You learn fast, speak plainly, and make hard topics feel survivable.","You can talk about a feeling instead of having it, and the steady Taurus manner makes the avoidance look like calm. Projects multiply because starting is a pleasure and choosing is not. Growth is one quiet hour with no audience, long enough for the Moon to say what the talking was covering."],"aries-gemini-gemini":["It is a habit, and you are the only one who thinks it is rude. Everyone else is relieved that someone is moving. You talk, you text, you offer an answer before the question has landed, and you are generous with ideas. The Gemini Moon and Gemini Rising make you a double talker in the best sense: what you feel and what you show both come out in words. The Aries Sun is the match under the paper, and it is what makes the talk lead somewhere.","The Moon and Rising share Gemini, so feeling and manner both run on Mercury, and both want novelty. The Aries Sun sextiles each, a friendly angle, and supplies what two air lights lack: a direction and a willingness to commit. Two mutable lights and one cardinal means you adapt with ease and start things on your own. What you lack is a fixed point. Everything in the chart moves, and the Sun has to find calm by choosing, not by waiting.","Fast thinking with nerve. You can learn anything, explain it, and then do it. You are funny and brave in the same breath, you adapt without losing yourself, and you make an uncertain room feel like a place where something is about to happen.","You may talk about a feeling in three ways and never have it once. Because the Moon and the face are both Gemini, there is no slower part to say stop, and the days fill with starts. Growth is choosing one thing and staying long enough to feel what it costs."],"aries-gemini-cancer":["The Aries voice is by the door, coat on, ready to go. The Gemini voice is at the window, narrating everything that passes. The Cancer one stands at the gate and decides who comes in. Visitors meet the gatekeeper first: tender, watchful, a little shy. They learn later that you are also fast, funny and curious about everything. The three are always arguing, and the argument is the energy that makes you good company.","Your Sun sextiles the Moon, so will and curiosity help each other, and the Gemini Moon gives the Aries fire a wider vocabulary. The difficulty is the Cancer Rising, which squares the Sun and sits a step from the Moon with little in common. The front is protective and slow to trust, while the light behind it is open and talkative. Cancer is ruled by the Moon, so the shell has moods, and you can seem to change your mind between one sentence and the next.","Warmth that talks. You make people feel welcome, you bring news and humour to a family, and you have a gift for putting feelings into words that others can use. You learn fast, and your courage helps shy people say what they mean.","The Gemini Moon explains and the Cancer front hides, so you can describe a feeling in detail and never let anyone close to it. The Aries Sun then acts on a mood that has already changed. Growth is picking one voice to speak for the whole house, for one evening, and meaning it."],"aries-gemini-leo":["It is a scene people remember: you at the end of a long table, a sheet of paper in your hands, a story going, and a stranger’s child wearing a crown by the second paragraph. You do it for fun and for the pleasure of being the one who makes the evening. The Leo Rising gives you the warmth of a host. The Gemini Moon gives you the story. The Aries Sun is why the table never went quiet.","An arc of ease: the Aries Sun trines Leo Rising, and the Gemini Moon sextiles both, so every light is on speaking terms with the other two. Two fire signs and one air, which means the air gives the fire a voice and the fire gives the air an audience. The Sun rules Leo, so your presentation and your purpose are the same person. The chart’s risk is that nothing resists you.","Charm that entertains and delivers. You can make a stranger feel like an old friend, make a story out of anything, and make a plan out of the story. You are generous with attention, quick to learn, and easy to follow.","When everything is easy, depth can feel like a detour. The Gemini Moon talks about a feeling instead of staying in it, and the Leo Rising makes the talking a show. Growth is an hour with no audience and no story, long enough to notice what you were about to say."],"aries-gemini-virgo":["It is the common misreading. You talk fast, change subject, answer three questions at once, and onlookers assume a nervy, busy mind that cannot settle. In truth you are comparing, sorting and double-checking all the time, and the speed is how a careful mind keeps up with an impatient Sun. Gemini and Virgo are both Mercury’s. You collect small details, correct a date in passing, and decide, quickly, what to do with them.","Mercury rules both your Gemini Moon and your Virgo Rising, so two of three lights think in the same quick, analytical way, and they square each other, arguing in the same language. The Aries Sun sextiles the Moon and stands a quincunx from the Rising. It is the one light that wants to do rather than weigh, and it is the one that can end the debate.","A quick mind that finishes. You learn fast, explain clearly, spot errors in passing and fix them in the next breath. Your humour is dry and accurate, your help is practical, and your courage to speak first lets others be careful.","Two lights run on Mercury, so the thinking never stops and the sorting is never done. You may rewrite a sentence five times and send it unfelt. Worry arrives as a to-do list. Growth is one decision made by instinct and left alone for a week."],"aries-gemini-libra":["The first minute at a party is your best hour. You are through the door, you have caught three names, made one joke and asked the question that gets the shy guest talking. People meet the Libra Rising, gracious and tasteful, and the Gemini Moon keeping the talk moving. The Aries Sun decides, around minute five, to say the thing nobody else will say, and to say it charmingly.","Two lights in air and one in fire, so the chart runs on conversation with the Sun as its spark. The Gemini Moon trines the Libra Rising, a natural ease between how you feel and how you appear, perhaps too easy to notice. The Sun sextiles the Moon, so wanting and needing cooperate when used, and opposes the Rising, a seesaw: you learn your own effect through other people’s reactions.","A social mind that can act. You read a room, find the common ground and then do something with it. Your humour is quick and kind, you can argue without spoiling the mood, and your introductions start friendships. People leave lighter, and better informed.","The talk is so easy that it can stand in for the deed. You can discuss a decision for three hours and make it in ten seconds out of impatience. The Libra front wants to please and the Gemini Moon wants to stay interesting, so you may agree with everyone in turn. Growth is finishing one sentence with “no”."],"aries-gemini-scorpio":["When something matters, you say it lightly. It comes out as a quip across the table, a throwaway line at the door, and you watch the face you said it to. If they catch it, you are quietly relieved. If they miss it, you were only joking. People meet the Scorpio Rising, steady and reading everyone, and the Gemini Moon behind it, quick and amused. The Aries Sun is the one that finally says it plainly.","A yod by sign: Sun and Moon are sextile, friendly and quick, and both stand a quincunx from the Scorpio Rising, which sits at the apex and is asked to adjust to both. The Rising keeps its depth and its secrets while the two lights talk and act at speed. Mars rules the Sun and, traditionally, the Rising, so gaze and will share a planet, and Mercury, the Moon’s ruler, translates the whole into wit.","Intensity you can talk to. You are quick, funny and observant, and you can say a difficult thing in a way people can hear. You read motives, tell stories with a point and keep real secrets. People trust you with the story and the silence both.","The wit is a vault door with a nice finish. You may deflect a question about feeling with a good line and call it honesty. The Aries Sun grows impatient and blurts the real thing at the wrong moment. Growth is answering one question a week with the unfunny version."],"aries-gemini-sagittarius":["Three voices live in your house. The Aries Sun is flint, striking a spark and wanting to begin. The Gemini Moon sits by the mirror asking whether that is quite true, and asking it again from the other side. The Sagittarius Rising is at the campfire telling the story, with the facts rounded a little in its favour. People hear mostly the third, a warm, funny, open-handed teller of tales, and sometimes catch the second muttering a correction.","Gemini and Sagittarius face each other across the wheel, so Moon and Rising make a seesaw between the fact and the meaning, the detail and the horizon. The Aries Sun sextiles the Moon and trines the Rising, so it cooperates with both and can end the debate by acting. Mercury rules the Moon and Jupiter the Rising, so the chart is fast, curious and generous.","A mind that tells and tests. You collect facts and turn them into stories people want to hear, you pick up languages and landscapes quickly, and you are funny in two registers. Your enthusiasm persuades and your doubt keeps you honest. People leave your table informed and cheered.","The seesaw never settles: you believe the story, then doubt it, then retell it. You may talk a plan to death, or decide before the evidence arrives. Both talking lights are happy to leave the quiet uncovered. Growth is finishing one idea before telling the next."],"aries-gemini-capricorn":["You are seen in a long meeting, face perfectly serious, folding the agenda into a paper boat under the table. Then you give the figure everyone needed, correct to the decimal, and the boat goes in your pocket. The Capricorn Rising wears the composure, the Gemini Moon needs the amusement to stay in the room, and the Aries Sun is the held sprint, ready to leave when the clock tower strikes.","Three different elements. The Sun sextiles the Gemini Moon, so wanting and needing cooperate when used, and squares the Capricorn Rising, cardinal against cardinal. The Moon stands a quincunx from the Rising, air and earth with nothing in common, so how you feel and how you seem have never quite been introduced. Mercury and Saturn rule between them wit under discipline. Expressive, fast-moving, mentally energised.","Wit with weight. You think quickly and deliver exactly, you make serious work enjoyable, and you have a dry humour that people repeat. You learn fast, explain clearly and keep deadlines. You can be trusted with the figures and with the joke.","The Gemini Moon needs variety and the Capricorn Rising needs credit, so you may take on three projects, finish two and resent the third. The seriousness can become a mask for restlessness. Growth is saying “I am bored” before you leave the room."],"aries-gemini-aquarius":["People think you are an ideas person who does not finish: all talk, a different plan every week, a lovely crossroads of conversation. They are wrong about the follow-through. Talking is how you think, and the Gemini Moon needs the crossroads, but the Aries Sun is a war drum in the background and the Aquarius Rising a signal tower, and what you say aloud on Tuesday is often built by Friday. You test ideas in speech first, because speech is cheap and fast.","An arc of ease: the Sun sextiles the Gemini Moon and the Aquarius Rising, and the Moon trines the Rising, air to air, so every light cooperates and the whole chart speaks one language. Mercury rules the Moon, and Saturn and Uranus the Rising. Expressive, fast-moving, mentally energised. Nothing in it resists, and so nothing in it insists on finishing.","Ideas that get tested. You think aloud, learn quickly, connect people and prove a thing on the spot. You are funny, generous with information and brave in public. People leave your company sharper, with three new names and an actual plan.","A chart without friction offers no pressure to finish. You may brilliantly begin eight things and finish two. The talk can stand in for the deed, and the signal for the signal being received. Growth is picking one idea each week and handing it to the Friday version of yourself."],"aries-gemini-pisces":["Dusk is your hour: the light going, the first drops of rain, a crossroads, and you standing there with the lantern still unlit, deciding which road you meant. The Pisces Rising is soft and receptive, a little faraway. The Gemini Moon is the quick mind arguing both roads at once. The Aries Sun is the held sprint, which will take one of them in a minute whether or not the argument is finished. People find you gentle and funny, and rarely guess how fast you can go.","The Sun sextiles the Gemini Moon, so wanting and needing cooperate when used, and stands a semi-sextile from the Pisces Rising, a neighbour with a blind spot. Moon and Rising square, both mutable, so mind and mood argue in the same restless style. Mercury rules the Moon, and Jupiter and Neptune the Rising, so facts and feeling keep trading places. Expressive, fast-moving, mentally energised.","Imagination with wit. You see what is not said and make a joke of it so it can be said. You learn fast, move easily between worlds and make strangers comfortable. Your enthusiasm is quick, and your gentleness makes it welcome.","The mutable Moon and Rising change their minds in turns, and the Aries Sun takes whichever road is nearest. You may start in one confusion and finish in another. Talk dissolves into mood. Growth is choosing the road at the crossroads and lighting the lantern after, not before."],"aries-cancer-aries":["The feeling lands low, in the stomach, and the answer rises through the shoulders and jaw. You stand square to whoever caused it, chin forward, heels planted, and say something louder and harder than the hurt that sent it. People meet the courage and the crackle and assume you are made of it. Then you go quiet, check that someone got home, ask what is for dinner and sit with a sore memory longer than you would admit. The shield is real. So is the soft thing it was built to guard.","Aries and Cancer square each other, and with all three lights cardinal, nothing here waits for permission. The Moon, at home in its own sign, is a tide that wants a harbour, and feeling comes slowly and from a long way off. The Aries Sun and Rising answer in half a second, so the reaction always outruns the feeling it protects. Anger arrives first and stands guard over a hurt that has not found words. When the lights agree, you defend the home you also keep. When they do not, you snap at the people you most want near.","Protection you can feel. You will cross a room, a city or an argument for someone being treated badly, and you will remember to ask whether they have eaten. You build loyalty fast and keep it, you make a home of any rented room, and you are brave in exactly the places where other people are only kind.","You can swing from charging to withdrawing so fast that nobody sees the middle, and so nobody knows you were hurt. The retreat may harden into a grudge with a long memory, kept warm in private. Care can also turn into management, because you have decided in advance what everyone needs. Growth is saying that hurt at the first twinge, before the fight and before the cave."],"aries-cancer-taurus":["Picture a loaf rising under a cloth in a kitchen at midnight: warm, patient, a little protected from the cold. That is the part of you people do not see at first. They meet the Taurus calm and the Aries nerve, someone who decides quickly and rarely looks rattled. Underneath is a Cancer Moon that wants the household fed, the family within reach and the day ending somewhere safe. You climb hard, but you are carrying something for someone else, and you would die before saying so.","Your Moon is at home in Cancer, so feeling is strong and fluent, and it squares your Aries Sun. The Sun wants to go out and win; the Moon wants to stay in and tend. The Taurus Rising sextiles the Moon, so your calm, practical manner is a genuine help, and it lets you do both: a steady provider’s face on a pushing, protective heart. When the square wins you feel torn. When the sextile does, you feel useful, which is your happiest state.","Provision with courage. You are the one who goes first and also the one who thinks about the supplies. Loyalty comes naturally, you protect the people inside your circle without making a speech, and your steadiness is a kind of shelter.","Because you give through action, you can start to count what you carry and quietly wait for it to be noticed. The Moon takes offence silently, and the Sun then pushes harder, which looks like work and feels like hurt. Growth is naming a need aloud, with the bread still warm."],"aries-cancer-gemini":["The voice in your head is not harsh. It is anxious, in the way of someone who loves the people they have just talked to. Was that kind, or only quick? Did I interrupt? Is everyone all right? People see a witty, mobile, ready person with a joke for the hall and a plan for the weekend. The Cancer Moon, at home in its own sign, then lies awake counting the words. You send the message, and an hour later you send a softer one.","Cancer is the Moon’s own sign, so feeling is strong and fluent, and it squares your Aries Sun, cardinal against cardinal, wanting and needing in a tug. Gemini Rising sextiles the Sun and keeps only a faint tie to the Moon, so the speed and the shyness meet badly. The tongue gets ahead of the tenderness. When the Mercury surface does its job it carries the feeling to the people who need it. When it does not, the wire hums and the hearth goes unvisited.","Warmth that can talk. You can say the kind thing quickly and remember it afterwards, you notice who is left out, and you make a family out of a room full of strangers. Your humour comforts, and your willingness to speak first helps shy people join in.","The Aries Sun acts first and the Cancer Moon takes the consequences home. You may apologise to cover a feeling you could simply name, or retreat into a long silence after a sharp word. Growth is letting one person see you need comfort, in plain words, before the evening ends."],"aries-cancer-cancer":["At twenty you cannot see that yet. You are ashamed of how fast you flare and how long you brood, and you assume one of them has to be the fake. Neither is. People meet a warm, careful face that reads their needs before they have spoken, and they are startled when the Aries Sun speaks plainly. You love by feeding and by guarding, and you are learning to do it without quietly counting what it costs.","The Moon and Rising both stand in Cancer, so feeling and manner are the same tender animal, and the Moon is at home in its own sign. The Aries Sun squares both, all three cardinal, so it is always asking to leave the shelter and win something. The result is a chart with one strong, fluent emotional language and a Sun that must learn to translate into it. When the Sun trusts the water, it moves with force. When it does not, it snaps.","Protective courage. You make people feel safe and then you defend them, you remember what matters to those you love, and you know when a room needs feeding. Your instincts are quick, and your care is the kind that actually arrives.","You hold the hurt for days and release it as a flash. The shell is so natural that the Sun, which wants to be bold, is almost always reacting to something it will not name. Growth is saying what hurts the same hour it hurts, and letting the shell stand open for a little while."],"aries-cancer-leo":["It is a true contradiction. You are the warmest, most visible figure at the party, and you are also the one who remembers every birthday and keeps the old photographs in a drawer. People meet the Leo Rising first: generous, warm, an arrival with some light in it. The Cancer Moon, at home in its own sign, is who you are after the guests leave. The Aries Sun is the nerve that lets you do both.","Cancer is the Moon’s own sign, so feeling is strong and fluent, and it squares your Aries Sun, wanting and needing in a tug. Leo Rising trines the Sun, which gives the fire a stage and takes the edge off the square. A semi-sextile stands between the Moon and the Rising, with a small blind spot: the front does not quite see the tender part. The Sun rules Leo, so the Rising speaks for the Sun, and the Moon waits in the wings.","A big heart with a public face. You can warm a room and mind it afterwards, you remember what matters to people and say so, and you protect your own with courage. Your loyalty is both theatrical and real.","The Leo front plays strength while the Cancer Moon stores the hurt. You may host a perfect evening and cry in the car. The Aries Sun then acts on the feeling the audience never saw. Growth is letting one person see you when the lights are off."],"aries-cancer-virgo":["The feeling lives in the stomach and the shoulders. Your shoulders lift, your belly tightens, and you start washing something. At midnight the Cancer Moon, at home in its own sign, goes back through the day word by word: what you said, who looked tired, whether you left the door unlocked. People meet the Virgo Rising, neat, modest and quietly helpful. The Aries Sun is the nerve that makes the first move and then spends the night sorting what it cost.","Cancer is the Moon’s own sign, so feeling is strong and fluent, and it squares your Aries Sun, wanting and needing in a tug. Virgo Rising sextiles the Moon, so the practical front gives the tender interior a way to help, and stands a quincunx from the Sun with little in common. The Rising is ruled by Mercury and organises the Moon’s care into tasks. When it works you feed people well. When it does not, you tidy at midnight.","Care that works. You notice who is tired, what is missing and what would help, and you do it without a fuss. Your courage defends the people you tend, and your attention to detail makes you the reliable centre of a family or a team.","Worry becomes weather, and the Aries Sun answers it with more activity. You may serve others to avoid asking for anything. The body keeps the account: a tight stomach, a clenched jaw. Growth is putting down the sieve and sitting still while someone else makes the tea."],"aries-cancer-libra":["A pearl begins as irritation, a grain of grit, and the oyster answers by wrapping it in layer after layer of light until nobody can find the grit. That is how you handle being hurt. The Cancer Moon is the shell, private and exact about who may come inside. The Libra Rising is the polished surface that greets visitors. The Aries Sun is the gauntlet kept in the drawer, and the glove goes on the moment someone you love is threatened.","A T-square by sign: Sun and Rising face each other, and the Moon squares both. The pressure travels round the triangle with no calm corner. The Moon is in its own sign, so feeling is strong and fluent. The Rising belongs to Venus, so it wants peace, and the Sun belongs to Mars, so it wants action. Whoever stands nearest tends to receive the third corner’s complaint. The tension is an engine, and an exhausting one.","Feeling with force behind it. You protect, you notice, and you act on what you sense. You are warm without being soft, polished without being false, and loyal in ways never announced. People in your circle grow braver and more comfortable at the same time.","Three corners, no rest. The Cancer Moon withdraws, the Libra Rising smooths it over, and the Aries Sun comes out swinging for an injury nobody was told about. You may keep a quiet ledger, then close the account in one afternoon. Growth is speaking the hurt in plain words while it is still only a grain."],"aries-cancer-scorpio":["Is this one safe, and how long will it take me to know? You ask that quietly about every new person, and sometimes about old ones. The Scorpio Rising watches them, steady and unreadable. The Cancer Moon needs the answer before it opens the door. The Aries Sun is the forge at first light: when the answer is yes, you move at once and without half measures, and by that night the lantern is in the window.","Two lights in water and one in fire. The Cancer Moon trines the Scorpio Rising, a natural ease between need and manner, so what you feel and how you guard it are nearly one thing. The Moon squares the Sun, so wanting and needing pull against each other, and Mars rules the Sun and, traditionally, the Rising, so front and fire share a planet. Decisive outside, private and intense beneath.","Loyalty with courage. When you let someone in you defend them without being asked, you remember what they said and what they needed, and you notice what is wrong before it is spoken. Your care is practical, your protection is real, and your trust, once given, holds.","The Cancer Moon and Scorpio Rising protect each other so well that nobody gets close, and the Aries Sun supplies the attack. You may test people without telling them. A small slight becomes a closed door. Growth is handing over the key before the test is passed, once, on purpose."],"aries-cancer-sagittarius":["At fifty you will see that you were never choosing between the kitchen and the horizon. In your twenties it felt like a daily fight: the Cancer Moon wanting everyone fed and safe, the Sagittarius Rising wanting the next country, the Aries Sun wanting to go before breakfast was over. You will come to see that you carried the kitchen with you everywhere, in your hands, and that people were warmed by the road you brought them.","The Cancer Moon is in its own sign, so feeling is strong and fluent, and it squares your Aries Sun, wanting and needing pulling against each other. It stands a quincunx from the Sagittarius Rising, five signs apart with nothing in common, while the Sun trines the Rising, so how you seem and who you are agree. Decisive on the surface, private and emotionally intense beneath, the most intense pairing and the least predictable.","Warmth with range. You make strangers feel at home and make home feel larger. You protect people and also push them to go, feed an army and then lead it, and your honesty comes with a meal. Your care has courage in it, and your courage has care.","The Moon needs the door locked and the Rising needs it open, and the Aries Sun leaves through the window. You may look after everyone and then vanish for a week. Moods swing between hospitality and escape. Growth is telling the people you love both halves in advance: I will come back, and I need to go."],"aries-cancer-capricorn":["You are the most dependable adult in the building and the one who cries in the car afterwards. Both are true, and neither is a performance. The Capricorn Rising is the composed, dry-humoured front people lean on. The Cancer Moon opposite it is the hearth light you keep for the people you love, strong and exact about who may come near it. The Aries Sun is the forge at first light, pushing both to start before anyone is ready.","A T-square by sign: the Cancer Moon and Capricorn Rising face each other across the wheel, and the Aries Sun squares both. Every corner is cardinal, so every corner wants to lead and the pressure never lets up. The Moon is in its own sign, so feeling is strong and fluent, and opposite the Rising, so home and duty pull in opposite directions. Decisive on the surface, private and intense beneath.","Strength with tenderness. You lead, you provide, you protect, and you remember what each person needs. Your standards are high and so is your care. People feel safe in your hands because you are both competent and kind.","Three corners, all pulling. You may work yourself empty for the people you love and then resent the work. Feelings arrive late and in private, and then they arrive hard. Growth is letting one person see the composure slip, before the car."],"aries-cancer-aquarius":["The feeling lives in the chest and the stomach, and your arms fold across it before you notice. You stand a little to one side, friendly, interested, composed. Then a friend is hurt and the arms drop and the water pours. The Aquarius Rising is the cool surface people meet. The Cancer Moon is the lantern in the window, kept lit for a very few. The Aries Sun is the first stroke of the brush, the move you make before anyone can tell what it cost.","The Cancer Moon is in its own sign, so feeling is strong and fluent, and it squares your Aries Sun, wanting and needing pulling against each other. It stands a quincunx from the Aquarius Rising, with nothing in common, so the tender interior and the cool front have never been properly introduced. The Sun sextiles the Rising. Decisive on the surface, private and intense beneath, the most intense pairing.","Care with range. You love fiercely and from a respectful distance, you notice who is cold and quietly warm them, and you act for strangers as readily as for friends. Your fairness has a heart in it, and your heart has a plan.","The cool Rising explains the Moon away, and the Aries Sun answers for it. You may say “I am fine” with a very convincing face. Tenderness leaks out as irritability, or as a sudden gift. Growth is naming the feeling to one friend while the arms are still crossed."],"aries-cancer-pisces":["Rain on a roof is the shelter and the sound of weather at the same time. That is how your feelings work, held and surrounded at once. The Cancer Moon is the roof, protective and exact about who may come in. The Pisces Rising is the rain, soft and everywhere, an estuary of other people’s moods. The Aries Sun is the flint and the spark in the dry room, the one thing in the picture that wants to go out into it.","Two lights in water and one in fire. The Cancer Moon is in its own sign, so feeling is strong and fluent, and it trines the Pisces Rising, so interior and front speak one tongue. The Moon squares the Aries Sun, wanting and needing pulling against each other, and the Sun is a semi-sextile from the Rising, a neighbour with a blind spot. Decisive on the surface, private and intense beneath, the most intense pairing.","Depth you can shelter in. You feel what others feel, make room for them and act on what you sense. You are protective, imaginative and brave, and your kindness has a spark in it. People come to you in bad weather.","Two water lights soak up everything, and the Aries Sun answers by lunging or leaving. You may be hurt long before anyone knows, and cross when they finally do. Moods are inherited from the room. Growth is stepping out of the rain on purpose, and saying so."],"aries-leo-aries":["The first ninety seconds of a party belong to you. You arrive already laughing, find the shy person by the coats, give the evening a direction and a dare, and by ten o’clock three strangers are doing something they had not planned. People meet generosity at full volume. They rarely see the one o’clock version, in the car, replaying whether you were noticed, whether anyone said thank you, whether the person you were kindest to was actually looking at you.","Leo trines Aries, fire to fire, so the Moon cheers whatever the Sun and Rising do, and that ease deserves some suspicion. Nothing here resists, which makes it easy to confuse applause with wellbeing. The Aries lights want to begin. The fixed Leo Moon wants to be seen beginning, and stays loyal to the show long after the Aries lights have moved on. Your Sun is exalted, an honoured guest, and the Moon has theatrical instincts of its own, so the house has two leads and one stage. You settle when the warmth is mutual.","Warmth with momentum. You get people moving and make them feel chosen while they move. You can lead a team, a toast or a rescue with the same open hands, you remember what makes each person feel brilliant and say it aloud, and your loyalty is as big as your entrance. You are the friend who arrives with a plan and a paper hat.","Because all three lights burn, nothing in the house is cool enough to keep the heat from turning into a need. You can mistake being watched for being loved, go quiet when someone’s attention drifts, and keep count of unanswered messages while insisting you do not mind. Growth is giving someone else the middle of the room and discovering you are still warm at the edge of it."],"aries-leo-taurus":["That is the habit people notice: the unbothered entrance, the warm voice, the way you take the good chair as if it had been waiting. What they see less is how much you need the applause. The Leo Moon wants warmth, colour and play, and the Aries Sun supplies the nerve to go and get them. The Taurus calm makes the wanting look like confidence, which it also is. You are generous with attention and hurt, privately, when it is not returned.","The Leo Moon trines your Sun, so fire talks to fire and your feelings and your will seldom argue. The trouble is the Rising. Taurus squares the Moon, two fixed signs facing each other, and each is certain about what it prefers. The Moon wants a stage and a fuss. The Rising wants a comfortable evening and no fuss at all. Venus rules the front and Mars rules the drive, so you look serene while two of your three lights quietly dig in.","Warmth you can build on. You make people feel chosen, you generate energy without burning anyone, and you stay loyal for decades. Your generosity is real and your taste is good. You can start a thing in a burst and see it through with style.","Being overlooked hurts more than you let on, and the Taurus calm hides the bruise until it hardens into a grudge. You may spend, stage or perform your way toward appreciation you could simply ask for. Growth is telling one person what you need to hear, plainly, before the quiet sets in."],"aries-leo-gemini":["The Aries one makes the decisions and wants to move. The Leo one wants the room warm and wants to be applauded for warming it. The Gemini one narrates, and is always three jokes ahead. You walk into a room and the room finds itself telling stories. The three rarely quarrel, because they want the same thing from different sides: to be seen, enjoyed and let loose. Dinner is a performance, and everyone has a part.","Your Sun trines the Moon, fire to fire, and both sextile Gemini Rising: an arc of ease, with Mercury giving voice to what Mars starts and the Leo Moon warms. Almost nothing here is in conflict. That is a gift and a hazard. When three lights agree, the chart moves toward applause and away from silence, and you may not know what you feel when no one is watching.","Charisma that works. You are funny, bold and warm in the same sentence, you tell a story so that every listener feels invited, and you can start a party, a plan or a rumour of a plan. Your generosity is catching, and so is your nerve.","Everything agrees, so there is little in you that says wait. You may fill the silence because silence feels like an empty theatre, and mistake attention for love. The wounds come when the audience goes home. Growth is spending an evening with no one watching and noticing what is left."],"aries-leo-cancer":["You are at the door with a covered dish, a little out of breath, already smiling. People see a warm, protective, slightly shy presence, and it is true as far as it goes. The Leo Moon wants thanks, colour and a story to tell about it. The Aries Sun wants to be the first one there. You give a great deal and you are quietly hurt when the giving goes unmarked, and the hurt shows up as a bright, hasty dignity.","Your Sun trines the Moon, fire to fire, so will and heart work together and you rarely feel torn about what you want. The Cancer Rising squares the Sun and sits a small step from the Moon, so the soft shell and the proud heart do not see each other well. The Rising wants to protect and hide, and the Moon wants to be seen. When they cooperate you give magnificently. When they do not, you give and then sulk.","Generosity with flame. You feed, defend and cheer, you make a household feel like a place worth coming home to, and you do it with real style. Your loyalty is warm and your courage is cheerful.","You may give in order to be seen, then be hurt when the seeing is slow. The Cancer front hides the wound and the Leo Moon makes a show of recovering. Growth is giving something where no one will ever know, and noticing that it was enough."],"aries-leo-leo":["The misreading is natural. You are warm, visible and proud, and you have a way of arriving that suggests you expect the room to turn. It does. But watch what you do with the attention: you hand it on. You introduce, you praise, you make the shy one laugh and the quiet one famous. The Aries Sun wants a fight worth having, and the Leo Moon and Leo Rising want everyone invited. The vanity is real and mostly beside the point.","Moon and Rising share Leo, so feeling and manner are the same warm animal, and the Sun rules both. The Aries Sun trines each, fire to fire, so there is little friction anywhere. All three lights are fire. The chart has one strong, bright voice and a Sun that doubles as its ruler. What is missing is shade: nothing in you naturally says stop, and nothing outside the blaze can tell you how it looks.","Warmth with authority. You make people feel chosen, lead without being asked, and give credit freely. Your confidence is infectious, your generosity is real, and your courage in front of a crowd lets other people be brave too.","Being overlooked wounds more than you say, and the Leo front turns the wound into a performance. You can mistake applause for love and ask the room for what one person could give. Growth is telling one friend what you need, plainly, with the lights up."],"aries-leo-virgo":["It is the hour you are most yourself: the tidy desk, the kettle, the herbs in their rows by the window, and a long day still to be won. People meet the Virgo Rising, someone neat, modest and watchful, and they see the preparation more than the nerve. The Leo Moon is the warmth behind it, wanting the work to be seen and appreciated. The Aries Sun is the banner in the wind, the one who goes out and plants it.","Your Sun trines the Leo Moon, fire to fire, so what you want and what you need pull together. Virgo Rising stands a quincunx from the Sun and a small step from the Moon, so the careful, modest front sees neither fire well. Mercury rules the Rising, and it edits what the fire does. When the three cooperate you are a brave person who works hard and is quietly proud of it. When they do not, you perform and then criticise the show.","Warmth with discipline. You start boldly, finish carefully and bring real heart to the work. You generate energy in a team, notice the details that make the difference, and praise people sincerely. Your quiet standards lift everyone near you.","The Leo Moon wants applause and the Virgo front is embarrassed to ask. You may work late hoping to be noticed and be hurt when you are not. The inner critic and the inner performer share one stage. Growth is saying what you did, out loud, without a disclaimer."],"aries-leo-libra":["When you are cornered, you get more generous. When you are tired, you get more gracious. When you are hurt, you open the best bottle, ask about everyone’s week and hand out compliments like torches, and nobody guesses anything is wrong. People meet the Libra Rising: tasteful, warm, attentive. The Leo Moon is the heart that wants to give and be seen giving. The Aries Sun is the flame itself.","Fire stands on both sides of the Libra Rising. The Sun trines the Leo Moon, so want and need pull the same way, and the Moon sextiles the Rising, so the heart and the front of house cooperate. Only the Sun opposes the Rising, a seesaw on which charm and drive take turns on top. Warmth is the common currency. The risk is a surface so lovely that nobody knows to ask what is behind it.","Warmth that organises. You gather people, make them feel chosen and give them something to do. Your generosity is real and your courage is public, so others borrow it. You lead by hospitality, and a decision from you feels like an invitation rather than an order.","The Leo Moon needs to be seen and loved and the Libra front hates to ask, so the need comes out as a gift with a hook in it. You may host the party to be sure you matter. Growth is saying “I would like you to notice me” without staging an evening first."],"aries-leo-scorpio":["Three voices live in your house. At the spearpoint, the Aries Sun wants to win, today, in public. By the bonfire, the Leo Moon wants to be loved out loud with the lights on. Down at the well, the Scorpio Rising wants nobody to know what you want. The result is a palace with every window lit and every shutter closed. People are drawn to the warmth and stopped by the gaze.","Fire trines fire: the Sun and the Leo Moon cooperate easily, so want and need pull together. The Scorpio Rising stands a quincunx from the Sun and a square from the Moon, so the guarded front argues with the bright heart. Mars rules the Sun and, traditionally, the Rising, so will and manner share a ruler. The friction between Moon and Rising is the engine of this chart, and its drama.","Charisma with weight. You warm a room and you also read it, you are generous and unfooled, and you command attention without chasing it. You love hard and protect those you love, and your authority is earned by being unafraid of difficult things.","The Leo Moon needs applause and the Scorpio Rising refuses to ask for it, so you may punish people for not noticing what you hid. Pride and secrecy share one throne. Growth is letting a trusted friend see the unlit room, and not performing in it."],"aries-leo-sagittarius":["You are seen at the head of a long table, standing, glass raised, toasting a stranger you met ten minutes earlier and meaning every word. The first bar of a fanfare is in your voice. The Sagittarius Rising makes the welcome wide, the Leo Moon wants the evening warm and a little grand, and the Aries Sun is the war drum underneath, so the party starts on time and the caravan leaves at dusk with everyone in it.","A grand trine by sign: Sun, Moon and Rising are three fire signs, each at ease with the others, a closed circuit that runs without friction. The Leo Moon trines the Sun and the Rising, so need and manner agree. Mars, the Sun and Jupiter, the three rulers, all burn warmly. The weakness of a closed circuit is that nothing outside it pushes back.","Generosity at scale. You bring people together, give them roles and send them away larger. Your confidence is warm, your humour is big and your loyalty is public. People trust you to lead because you also pour the drinks.","Nothing in the chart says no. The ease is so complete that you may not notice when you have overpromised, outshone a friend or spent the budget. Pride and optimism agree with each other. Growth is asking one person who is not charmed by you what they think, and listening to the end."],"aries-leo-capricorn":["People take you for the serious one: composed, correct, a little severe, dry in humour, someone to trust with the budget. They are right about the budget. They are wrong about the rest. The Leo Moon is a bonfire kept in a cellar, wanting to be generous, admired and loved out loud. The Aries Sun is the red thread running through it, and when the day is done and the ledger closed you are warm, theatrical and surprisingly funny.","Fire trines fire: the Sun trines the Leo Moon, so want and need pull the same way. The Capricorn Rising squares the Sun, cardinal against cardinal, and stands a quincunx from the Moon, with nothing in common, so the formal front fits neither fire. Saturn rules the Rising and the Sun rules the Moon, so authority and warmth have to learn each other’s language. Amplified passion and drive.","Warmth with authority. You earn respect and then spend it generously. You lead properly, give lavishly and remember anniversaries. People who know you well know a loyal, funny, big-hearted friend under the suit, and the suit lets you keep that up for decades.","The Leo Moon wants applause and the Capricorn Rising finds asking for it undignified, so you may wait for recognition that never arrives and then be stung. Pride and propriety share one throne. Growth is saying “I did that, and I am proud of it” in your normal voice."],"aries-leo-aquarius":["The hour after the applause fades is yours: the house lights up, the crowd filing out, the held sprint of the evening finally over. This is when you thank the crew by name, mean it, and stack a chair. The Leo Moon wanted every minute in the light. The Aquarius Rising, opposite it, wants the group to have its share, and quietly believes the technician at the mixing desk is the real story. The Aries Sun lit the whole evening.","Fire trines fire: the Sun trines the Leo Moon, so want and need pull together. The Leo Moon stands opposite the Aquarius Rising, so the seesaw is the star and the audience, the one and the many. The Sun sextiles the Rising. Amplified passion, confidence and drive, balanced by a cool, friendly, egalitarian front, which is a lasting lesson in sharing the stage.","Charisma with fairness. You light up a room and then make sure everyone is in it. You are generous, brave and original, and you lead from the front and then step aside. People feel included in your success, because you included them.","The Leo Moon wants to be loved personally and the Aquarius Rising wants to be admired in general, so you may be warm to a crowd and distant to a friend. You may perform detachment. Growth is letting one friend see you wanting the applause, and giving it to them."],"aries-leo-pisces":["You make your entrance softly, in fog. When you are cornered, you go quiet and warm. When you are tired, you get more generous. When you are delighted, you light up like a bonfire seen through mist, large, golden and a little hard to place. The Pisces Rising is the fog: gentle, receptive, a little faraway. The Leo Moon is the fire behind it, wanting to give and be seen giving. The Aries Sun is the red thread through both.","Fire trines fire: the Sun trines the Leo Moon, so want and need pull together. The Pisces Rising is a semi-sextile from the Sun and a quincunx from the Moon, with nothing in common, so the soft front fits neither fire and softens both. Jupiter and Neptune rule the Rising, and the Sun rules the Moon. Amplified passion and drive, behind a gentle mist.","Warmth that does not crush. You are generous, dramatic and kind, and people feel the heat without being burned. You lead by inspiring rather than pushing, and you remember who needed to be seen. Your courage comes with a gentleness that makes it easier to follow.","The Leo Moon wants applause and the Pisces Rising will not ask, so you may fade into the fog hoping to be found. Pride hides in modesty. The Aries Sun may flare when nobody came looking. Growth is stepping out of the mist once and saying “look”."],"aries-virgo-aries":["A blacksmith swings a heavy hammer all afternoon and then picks up the finest file in the shop to take the burr off a single hinge. That is the sequence of you. The world meets the hammer: decisive, brisk, a little brusque, already moving. The file comes later and in private, when you replay what you said, tidy the desk, redo the list and quietly fix the thing someone else got wrong. Your worry is a kind of workmanship. It is also the only part of you that ever sits still.","Aries and Virgo are a quincunx, five signs apart and strangers by element and mode, so the Moon and the Sun and Rising behave like colleagues who share a building and have never been introduced. The Aries pair move first and explain never. The Virgo Moon is mutable, an editor by nature, and audits the work after the deadline, finding the three things that could have been better. Mars drives, Mercury annotates. You settle when the two agree on a division of labour: act in the daylight, repair at night, and sit down once in between.","Competence in motion. You can fix a problem while still inside it, and you will build the first version, spot its flaw and finish the second before others have chosen a font. You are the practical ally in a crisis. Your courage comes with a checklist, and your help turns up as a repaired thing rather than a speech about one.","The inner critic does its sentencing after the Aries lights have committed the act. You can rush, scold yourself for rushing, then hold everyone else to the same audit, and the correction often lands on a person who only wanted to be thanked. Growth is letting the first draft count as finished, and treating the repair as craft instead of punishment."],"aries-virgo-taurus":["Is it ready, or am I only tired of waiting? You ask it in the car, over a half-finished job, at the end of a long week. People see someone calm, capable and quietly useful, the one who mends the thing nobody asked about. They do not see the Aries Sun pacing behind it, impatient to move, or the Virgo Moon grading the work as it goes. You do real work, and you rarely feel finished.","Sun and Moon sit a quincunx apart, five signs from each other with nothing in common. The Sun wants to charge and the Moon wants to check, and it is the one angle in your chart that keeps asking for adjustment. Taurus Rising trines the Moon, both earth, so your front and your feeling agree on routine, craft and getting things right. That earth alliance gives you steadiness. It also means the Sun is sometimes outvoted by two careful signs.","Competence with courage. You will start the hard task and tidy the mess it leaves. Your standards are high without being theatrical, your help arrives as a finished thing rather than a promise, and people learn that you do exactly what you said you would.","The inner critic runs through the Moon and borrows the Aries speed as a stick: why is it not done, why was it not better. You can work past hunger and tiredness and call it discipline. Growth is stopping at good enough on purpose and eating a proper meal while the list stays unfinished."],"aries-virgo-gemini":["At twenty you cannot see it. You think the critic in your head is just being accurate, and you believe being useful and being loved are the same thing. People meet a quick, funny, dexterous mind, someone who is always doing three things well. They miss the Aries Sun’s nerve and the Virgo Moon’s worry, which is why you keep working after the work is done. You will learn that rest was part of the job.","Mercury rules both your Virgo Moon and your Gemini Rising, so two of your three lights think in the same quick, analytical way. They are also square, which means they argue in the same language. The Moon criticises what the Rising has just said. Your Sun, a quincunx from the Moon, wants to charge on and not stop to check, and sextiles the Rising. It is the one light in the chart with no one to talk to.","A fast mind that does the work. You can see what is wrong, say it kindly, and fix it before lunch. Your humour is dry and exact, your help arrives finished, and when you have chosen a thing you finish it with a care few people notice and many rely on.","Two lights run on Mercury, so the inner critic and the outer talker speak the same language and rarely give you a silent minute. You can edit your own life as it happens. Growth is leaving one thing imperfect on purpose, and noticing that nothing falls over."],"aries-virgo-cancer":["It is a true contradiction, and it confuses everyone who meets you. You are tender enough to cry at a stranger’s story and exacting enough to reorganise their kitchen while they do. People meet the Cancer Rising: soft, watchful, quick to help. The Virgo Moon does the helping with a list. The Aries Sun supplies the nerve to say, kindly, that the sauce needs salt. You are not unkind. Care, to you, is precision, and mercy is a job done well.","The Sun and the Moon sit a quincunx apart, five signs from each other with nothing in common, so what you want and what you need keep asking each other to adjust. Cancer Rising squares the Sun and sextiles the Moon, so the protective front agrees with the practical Moon and quarrels with the headstrong Sun. Cancer is ruled by the Moon, so your tenderness takes its time, while the Sun wants to charge and be done.","Care that works. You notice what is needed, do it without fuss, and leave things better than you found them. You protect your people practically and bravely, and your standards come out as help instead of judgement. Competent warmth is rarer than most people know.","The critic and the carer are close cousins, and the Aries Sun can turn a correction into an attack. You may fix what people only wanted you to hear. Worry becomes weather. Growth is sitting beside someone’s trouble without improving it, for an hour."],"aries-virgo-leo":["The body gives you away. When something matters you stand taller, your jaw sets, and your hands go to whatever needs tidying. People meet the Leo Rising, a warm and orderly presence, someone who dresses for the occasion and arrives on time. The Virgo Moon is behind it, grading the performance as it happens. The Aries Sun is the part that wants to do it anyway. You hold yourself to a standard that suits the stage and wears the person.","The Sun trines Leo Rising, fire to fire, so will and presentation work easily together. The Moon is a quincunx from the Sun, with nothing in common, so what you want and what you need keep asking each other to adjust. A semi-sextile stands between the Moon and the Rising, a small blind spot. The Sun rules Leo, so the Rising is the Sun’s own face. Two fire lights lead, and the earth Moon adds the standards.","Polish with courage. You bring warmth and precision to the same job, and you finish what you start to a higher standard than anyone asked. People feel looked after by someone who notices details and does something about them. Your work has dignity.","The inner critic watches from the wings and the Leo front never lets it show. You may rehearse a feeling until it is correct, and miss the one that was real. Growth is a task done badly on purpose, in public, and survived."],"aries-virgo-virgo":["Picture the workbench: every tool in its outline, a lamp, a basket of things that nearly work. That is where the Virgo Moon and Virgo Rising live, sorting the harvest into what can be mended and what can go. People meet someone modest and useful, an expert in small repairs. The Aries Sun is the surprise: it is the one who strides in and says, we are doing this today, and gets the first screw out before the others have found their glasses.","Moon and Rising share Virgo, so feeling and manner are the same careful animal, and Mercury rules both. The Aries Sun stands a quincunx from each, five signs away with nothing in common, so the fire is the odd one out in its own house. It wants to charge and the other two want to check. When it works you have a bold leader and a meticulous staff of two. When it does not, the Sun sulks.","Precision with nerve. You see exactly what is wrong and you act on it, you finish what you begin, and you quietly improve everything you touch. Your reliability is real and your courage is practical. People hand you the hard job and go home.","Two Virgo lights audit the Sun at every step, so the nerve has to argue its way out of a long list. You may fix a small thing to avoid a large one. Rest feels like a fault. Growth is leaving the bench for an afternoon, and letting something stay broken until Monday."],"aries-virgo-libra":["Did I do that right, did it look right, and why am I already starting the next thing? Those are your questions, usually on the way home. The Libra Rising is the pressed linen, gracious and neatly turned out. The Virgo Moon goes back over the day with a pencil, correcting small errors nobody noticed. The Aries Sun did it all before breakfast and would, quietly, like some credit.","Sun and Moon stand a quincunx, five signs apart with nothing in common, so what you do and what you need keep being introduced and never become friends. The Libra Rising opposes the Sun, a seesaw, and sits a semi-sextile from the Moon, a neighbour that barely sees it. Venus shapes the surface, Mercury the interior, Mars the drive. The front is easy, the middle is exacting, and the nerve is bold.","Taste with standards. You make things well and make them pleasant, finish what you begin and notice the detail that matters. You are fair, helpful and brave in small, useful ways. People ask you to look something over because you will be both honest and kind about it.","The Virgo Moon audits and the Libra Rising keeps up appearances, so you can fix everything except the thing you are actually worried about. You may postpone an argument until the facts are tidy, by which time the Aries Sun has lost interest. Growth is sending it at ninety percent and letting the room be imperfect."],"aries-virgo-scorpio":["At fifty you will see that the thing you worked hardest to repair was yourself. In your twenties the Virgo Moon fixed, tidied and corrected, and the Scorpio Rising watched everyone with a steady, unreadable gaze, while the Aries Sun stood on the ledge, impatient to go. You will realise that the watching and the fixing were one long way of staying safe, that the ram was always allowed to jump, and that ash was never the end of anything.","A yod by sign: the Virgo Moon and Scorpio Rising are sextile, friendly with one another, and both stand a quincunx from the Aries Sun, which sits at the far point. The Sun keeps being asked to adjust to two lights that cooperate and do not need it. Mars rules the Sun and, traditionally, the Rising. Mercury, the Moon’s ruler, is the clerk who files what the other two cannot say.","Precision with depth. You see what is wrong and what is hidden, and you can act. You fix, protect and finish. People trust your discretion and your care, and you have a rare patience for mending things others would abandon. Your courage is quiet and exact.","Sorting becomes a way of avoiding feeling. You may analyse a pain until it is a list, then stand guard over the list. The Aries Sun, at the apex of the yod, is rarely consulted and sometimes explodes. Growth is leaving one problem unsolved overnight and noticing that you survive."],"aries-virgo-sagittarius":["You are a wild, restless, open-road person who alphabetises the spice rack, and both are true. The first stroke of the brush, the first mile of the road, is the Aries Sun. The Sagittarius Rising is the laugh and the news. The Virgo Moon sorts the harvest in the evening, checks the tyre pressure and labels the jars before you leave. People see the adventure. Your friends know the list.","The Sun trines the Rising, so how you seem and who you are agree. The Virgo Moon stands a quincunx from the Sun, with nothing in common, and a square from the Rising: mutable earth against mutable fire, one modality with two different appetites. Mercury rules the Moon and Jupiter the Rising, so detail argues with meaning. Bold outside, patient and cautious underneath.","Adventure that comes home safe. You start boldly, prepare well and notice what could go wrong while the laughter is still going. You turn a wild idea into a working plan, fix what breaks on the road and share what you learned. People ask you along because the trip actually happens.","The Virgo Moon audits the Sagittarius Rising’s promises, and the Aries Sun acts before the audit is done. You may undermine your own enthusiasm with a list, then resent the list. Worry arrives dressed as practicality. Growth is leaving one road unmapped and one jar unlabelled, on purpose."],"aries-virgo-capricorn":["The feeling goes to the hands and the lower back. The more it matters, the straighter you stand and the busier your hands get: weeding, sorting, folding, correcting. People meet the Capricorn Rising, composed and unhurried, and the Virgo Moon behind it, tending the herb garden in rows. The Aries Sun is the forge at first light, which starts the day before anyone else is up and sets the pace of a long ascent.","Two earth lights and one fire. The Virgo Moon trines the Capricorn Rising, so interior and front agree about order, effort and standards. The Aries Sun squares the Rising, cardinal against cardinal, and stands a quincunx from the Moon, with nothing in common. Mercury and Saturn run the chart, with Mars as the engine, so the result is bold outside, patient and cautious underneath, action tempered by practicality.","Craft with nerve. You begin early, work cleanly and finish what you started. You improve everything you touch and ask little credit. Your courage is practical, your standards are high and your care is exact, so people hand you the real work.","Two earth lights outvote the Sun, so a bold impulse is vetted until it is no longer bold. You may criticise yourself for an hour of rest. The body keeps the account in the back and the hands. Growth is stopping work because the day is lovely, and not making it up later."],"aries-virgo-aquarius":["After a night of lightning, in the cold morning air, the farmer walks the rows sorting the harvest into what survived and what did not. That is how you handle a shock. The Aquarius Rising is the strange light in the sky, cool and a little ahead of the day. The Virgo Moon is the notebook in the farmer’s pocket, careful and exact. The Aries Sun was out before dawn, already working, and has not yet said how frightening the storm was.","A yod by sign: the Aries Sun and Aquarius Rising are sextile, friendly with each other, and both stand a quincunx from the Virgo Moon, at the far point, five signs away with nothing in common. The Moon keeps being asked to adjust to two lights that cooperate and do not need it. Bold outside, patient and cautious underneath, with the interior as the tireless adjuster.","Original thinking with method. You see what others miss and record it so it can be used. You start boldly, work carefully and explain clearly. You handle a crisis with a list and a kind word. People trust your odd ideas because you check them.","The Virgo Moon at the apex does all the adjusting, and the sextile pair never notices the cost. You may worry in private while appearing cool, and fix other people’s systems while your own tires. Growth is letting a small mess stand for an evening, unlogged."],"aries-virgo-pisces":["Is this my confusion, or is the situation actually confusing? You ask it at the workbench in the evening, with the gate unlatched and a half-remembered dream still in the room. The Virgo Moon takes inventory: what is known, what is guessed, what can be fixed. The Pisces Rising, opposite it, is the mist you keep trying to catalogue. The Aries Sun is the one who finally walks out of the door and does something about it.","The Virgo Moon and Pisces Rising face each other across the wheel, a seesaw of order and flow, detail and surrender, with Mercury and Neptune in one chart. The Sun is a quincunx from the Moon, with nothing in common, and a semi-sextile from the Rising, a neighbour with a blind spot, so the fire is the odd one out in both directions. Bold outside, patient and cautious underneath.","Imagination with method. You feel the whole of a situation and then find the practical next step. You are kind, exact and brave, you can sort a crisis into parts, and you can hold a confused friend steady. People trust you to help and not only to sympathise.","The Virgo Moon criticises the Pisces Rising’s vagueness, and the Pisces Rising dissolves the Moon’s lists. You may worry about worry. The Aries Sun leaves the room to escape both. Growth is allowing one thing to stay unclear, and acting on the ninety percent you do know."],"aries-libra-aries":["When you are cornered you do two things, in order. You say exactly what you think, in plain words, with your chin up. Then you ask whether that was too much, whether everyone is all right, whether there was a way to say it that nobody would mind. “Whatever you prefer” lasts about nine seconds before the preference comes out. People meet someone bold and bright, and are surprised to learn you cannot sit in a room that has gone cold between two people, and will cross it to fix it.","Your Libra Moon sits directly opposite the Aries Sun and Rising, so the chart is a seesaw with two lights on one end and one on the other. The Aries side says me, now, my way. The Moon says us, fairly, together. Libra needs a companion in order to feel at all, which means you tend to find your missing half in other people: partners who seem too forceful or too hesitant to bear. Some of what you notice in them is your own other end. Rest comes when the ends take turns.","Courage with manners. You can start the hard conversation and leave the other person’s dignity intact. You see the fairness in a stubborn situation quickly and are bold enough to act on it. People feel pushed and respected at once, and few can be this direct and leave a room lighter rather than bruised.","The seesaw can swing from seizing the lead to handing it over before anyone has agreed. You may decide fast, then wait for a partner to do the weighing, and resent them when they weigh differently. Or you hold back the real want to keep the peace, and it returns later as sharpness. Growth is naming the want first and the fairness second, and trusting the bond to survive both."],"aries-libra-taurus":["One stands by the door with a coat on, ready to go and do the thing. One keeps asking whether everyone has eaten and whether anybody is upset. One has already set the table and sees no reason to move. You live between them, and visitors meet the table-setter: warm, composed, a little slow to rise. The door-stander sulks in the hall. The peacemaker keeps the soup hot. When the three agree, you are hard to beat and delightful company.","Sun and Moon face each other across the wheel, an opposition, so what you do and what you need see all of each other and seldom meet in the middle. Venus rules both the Libra Moon and the Taurus Rising, so two of the three voices share a sweetness and a taste for peace. That leaves the Sun outnumbered. It explains the pattern: a strong will in a house that prefers pleasant evenings.","A fighter who can host. You can disagree and keep the dinner going, hold a line without raising your voice, and make a hard conversation feel like a courtesy. People trust that you will be fair, and your good taste makes difficult things easier to attend.","The Libra Moon avoids a quarrel the Aries Sun would settle in a minute, and the Taurus calm backs it up. Resentment sits at the table unspoken until it speaks all at once. Growth is saying the unwelcome sentence while the soup is still warm, and trusting the friendship to hold it."],"aries-libra-gemini":["Watch you at a doorway. You hold it open, you say hello, and you know every name before it is offered. People meet the Gemini Rising: quick, curious, a face full of interest. The Libra Moon wants every guest to feel at ease and keeps the bell ringing. Behind both is the Aries Sun, which is judging the room by whether anything is going to happen in it, and which wants to be out the door before the small talk runs out.","Sun and Moon face each other across the wheel, an opposition, so what you do and what you need see each other clearly and rarely settle. The Moon trines Gemini Rising, both air, so feeling and manner flow together and make you easy company. That trine is the reason the opposition is bearable. The pleasing arrives through the front door, and the Sun comes in by the back.","Charm with a spine. You can host, argue, flatter and tell the truth without losing anyone. You listen as if it matters, and you see both sides faster than the people standing on them. When it comes to a decision, you make it.","The Libra Moon will keep the peace by agreeing, and the Gemini voice makes the agreement sound sincere. The Aries Sun then resents the compromise. Decisions can be put off while you gather one more opinion. Growth is saying the unwelcome thing to the one person who needs to hear it, with the bell still ringing."],"aries-libra-cancer":["The misreading is easy to make. You look soft, tactful, anxious that everyone is comfortable, and you have the sweet voice of someone who would never start an argument. You will not start one. But the Aries Sun does finish them, and the Libra Moon is a better observer of unfairness than anyone supposes. People who mistake your courtesy for weakness discover that the courtesy was a choice, and that you had the flint in your pocket the whole time.","Sun and Moon face each other across the wheel, and the Cancer Rising squares both of them: a T-square by sign, with the Rising at the corner taking the pressure. All three lights are cardinal, so each one wants to lead. That is the pressure behind your calm. Cancer is ruled by the Moon, so mood comes in waves, and the pull between will and company, between going and staying, arrives through the shell.","Peace with a spine. You can hold a room together, see both sides, and then say the one hard thing that settles it. You are fair under pressure and warm in disagreement, and people trust you because they have seen you act.","Under a T-square the corner often does the most work, and you can bear the tension for others until you are exhausted. The Libra Moon avoids the fight, the Cancer front hides the cost, and the Aries Sun waits for a moment to blow. Growth is choosing one conflict a month to have openly."],"aries-libra-leo":["The table is set, the music is chosen, and you are checking your face in the hall mirror. This is the hour you are most yourself. People meet the Leo Rising: warm, theatrical, a host with a sense of occasion. The Libra Moon wants everyone to arrive to a lovely room and leave feeling seen, and it keeps the evening fair. The Aries Sun is the nerve behind it, and the reason you will open the door before the second knock.","Sun and Moon face each other across the wheel, an opposition, so what you do and what you need see each other clearly and rarely settle. The Moon sextiles Leo Rising, which gives the feeling a graceful way to appear, and the Sun trines the Rising, so the front is an easy ally to both. The Sun rules Leo. The arrangement works best in company: the duet needs a second voice.","Warmth with fairness. You make a room feel gracious and then keep it that way, you see both sides without losing your own, and you charm without condescension. People relax around you and are surprised by how decisive you can be.","The Libra Moon will keep the peace by agreeing, the Leo front performs the agreement beautifully, and the Aries Sun resents it afterwards. You may avoid a quarrel to protect the evening. Growth is saying the unwelcome thing before the guests arrive, not after they leave."],"aries-libra-virgo":["It is a habit your family knows. A rising voice means the cushions get plumped and the cups get washed, and the more furious you are, the better the kitchen looks. People meet the Virgo Rising, neat, modest and observant, and the Libra Moon wants everyone comfortable and fairly treated. Both are gentle on the surface. The Aries Sun is the war drum under it, steady, patient for a while, and then very loud.","Sun and Moon face each other across the wheel, an opposition, so what you do and what you need see each other clearly and rarely settle. Virgo Rising stands a quincunx from the Sun and a small step from the Moon. Mercury rules the Rising, so a calm, analytical front handles what the Moon feels and the Sun wants. The three seldom speak plainly to each other. The pressure leaks out as tidiness.","Fair-minded competence. You see both sides, fix what is broken and say so politely, and you can be firm without being cruel. People trust you to be even-handed and also to finish. Your courage arrives when it is needed, and not before.","The Libra Moon avoids the quarrel and the Virgo front tidies the evidence, so the real grievance goes unsaid. Then the Aries Sun finishes the argument in one sentence. Growth is naming the irritation while it is still small, before you have cleaned the whole house."],"aries-libra-libra":["Three voices live in your house. In the forge at first light, the Aries Sun wants to hit something and begin. In the salon, the Libra Moon asks whether everyone is comfortable and whether it was fair. At the door, the Libra Rising greets guests with immaculate manners. The last two speak one language and tend to outvote the first. Others see velvet, and sometimes find a hammer in it.","Moon and Rising share Libra, so feeling and manner are one gracious animal ruled by Venus, and the Aries Sun faces both across the wheel: a seesaw with one weight on each side. The fire is the lone dissenter. You often meet it through other people, a partner or rival who acts as fast as you secretly would. The lesson is balance. The hammer and the velvet need each other.","Grace with a spine. You sense what each side wants, you can broker a settlement, and you can also be the one who ends a standoff by acting. You keep your promises and your poise, make beautiful things happen on time, and stay fair even when angry.","Two Libra lights vote for peace, and the Aries Sun can only win by ambush. You may put off a decision until a partner makes it for you, then resent the result. You can lose your own opinion while weighing everyone else’s. Growth is deciding first, asking second, and bearing a small unpopular outcome."],"aries-libra-scorpio":["You are seen at a table with two chairs facing, composing something courteous, crossing out a line and starting again. The Libra Moon wants the exchange to be fair and kind. The Scorpio Rising stands behind the pen, reading every word for what it gives away. The Aries Sun keeps a second letter in the drawer, blunter and sealed, which it sometimes sends. People receive the polite one and feel, vaguely, the pressure of the other.","Sun and Moon are in opposition, a seesaw between acting and weighing, and the Scorpio Rising is a quincunx from the Sun and a semi-sextile from the Moon, so the front fits neither neatly. Mars rules the Sun and, traditionally, the Rising, so will and gaze are close kin. Venus rules the Moon, so what you need is harmony and what you show is intensity. They rarely agree on how to say anything.","Tact with teeth. You are fair, observant and brave, you can negotiate, and you know when not to. You see both sides and the motives beneath them, and you hold a line without raising your voice. People bring you their disputes because you will take them seriously.","The Libra Moon avoids the quarrel, the Scorpio Rising files the grievance, and the Aries Sun finally posts the blunt letter. You may be gracious for months and then end something in a sentence. Growth is sending the first letter, the honest one, while it is still small."],"aries-libra-sagittarius":["People think you are the easy one: sunny, sociable, unbothered, a good laugh and a good listener. They are half right. The Sagittarius Rising brings the open hand and the story. The Libra Moon is quietly at work all the time on whether everyone is comfortable, whether it was fair, whether anyone was left out. Under the chandeliers a campfire is burning, and the Aries Sun is the one who will walk out when fairness fails.","Sun and Moon stand in opposition, a seesaw between acting and weighing, and the Libra Moon sextiles the Sagittarius Rising, air and fire, so interior and front are friends. The Sun trines the Rising. Venus rules the Moon and Jupiter the Rising, so it is a generous, sociable chart. Others often carry the patience you do not show, and you learn balance by watching them.","Warmth with fairness. You welcome everyone, see all sides and still say what you think. You tell good stories, make good introductions and settle a quarrel by laughing at it. Your courage is friendly, and your friendliness has a spine.","The Libra Moon avoids the quarrel, the Sagittarius Rising jokes about it, and the Aries Sun leaves the room. You may be hard to pin down on anything that matters. A decision can wait for someone else to make it. Growth is saying the unwelcome thing once, kindly, instead of joking about it twice."],"aries-libra-capricorn":["The hour before signing is yours: the contract, the lease, the wedding band still in its box, the pen not yet picked up. Under cathedral stone the Libra Moon asks whether it is fair to everyone, the Capricorn Rising asks whether it will hold, and the Aries Sun, spearpoint in hand, asks why you have not signed yet. People see a very composed, courteous adult. You know you have been up since four weighing it.","A T-square by sign: Sun and Moon face each other across the wheel, and the Capricorn Rising squares both. All three are cardinal, so every corner wants to lead and none will give way, and the pressure is constant. Venus rules the Moon and Saturn the Rising, so charm and duty hold the middle. Expressive, fast-moving, mentally energised, and rarely at rest.","Commitment with grace. You weigh both sides, keep your promises and make firm decisions look gentle. You are fair, formal and courageous, and your word, once given, holds. People bring you the hard negotiation because you are polite, patient and unmovable.","The Libra Moon delays, the Capricorn Rising demands certainty, and the Aries Sun cannot bear either. You may refuse to decide until the cost of not deciding is the decision. Growth is signing at ninety percent sure, and learning to live inside the other ten."],"aries-libra-aquarius":["When you are cornered, you say let us be fair about this. You mean: I am furious, and I am also right. When you are tired you agree to the first reasonable offer. When you are delighted you invite everyone into the glass house, a wedding band on a hand, an idea on the table, and let them look. The Aquarius Rising is cool and friendly, the Libra Moon is the diplomat, and the Aries Sun is the war drum inside the glass.","Sun and Moon stand in opposition, a seesaw between acting and weighing. The Libra Moon trines the Aquarius Rising, air to air, so interior and front are fluent and easy together, and the Sun sextiles the Rising, so fire and air cooperate. Venus rules the Moon, Saturn and Uranus the Rising. Expressive, fast-moving, mentally energised, and very hard to rattle in public.","Fairness with force. You listen to all sides, propose something workable and then see it through. You are friendly, principled and brave, and you make a hard conversation feel like a shared project. People trust your fairness because you can also be angry.","The Libra Moon and Aquarius Rising agree so well that the Aries Sun’s anger has no listener until it shatters the glass. You may defer, discuss and weigh until a partner takes the decision. Growth is stating the grievance as a plain “I am angry” before it becomes a principle."],"aries-libra-pisces":["Three voices live in your house. The Aries Sun is out in the cold morning air, wanting a fight it can win and be done with. The Libra Moon sits between two chairs facing, wanting a peace everyone can sign. The Pisces Rising, salt on its skin, wants to dissolve and let the water decide. People meet the third, soft, kind and drifting, and are surprised by the first and moved by the second.","Sun and Moon stand in opposition, a seesaw between acting and weighing, and the Pisces Rising is a semi-sextile from the Sun and a quincunx from the Moon, so the soft front fits neither well. Venus rules the Moon, and Jupiter and Neptune the Rising, so charm and compassion are the common coin. Expressive, fast-moving, mentally energised, and much more decided than it looks.","Diplomacy with feeling. You sense what each side needs, put it gently and hold the peace until it takes. You are kind, brave and fair, and you can stand between two people without taking a side. Your tact is real, and so is your temper.","The Libra Moon avoids the quarrel, the Pisces Rising absorbs it, and the Aries Sun finally ends it in one sentence. You may be agreeable for months. Your own wants float away in the wash. Growth is stating one preference a day, out loud, before anyone asks."],"aries-scorpio-aries":["Who here has earned the real version? You ask it silently at every table, in a voice that never reaches your face. Your face is busy being open: forthright, quick, funny, willing to pick the fight and laugh after it. All of that is true. It is also the front porch. Behind it is a room you keep locked, and you remember, with unwelcome exactness, every time a door was closed on you.","Aries and Scorpio are a quincunx, so the Moon has never quite been introduced to the Sun and Rising. Yet Mars rules the Aries pair and, in the old scheme, the Moon’s sign too, so they share a planet and speak different dialects of it. In Aries, Mars is the sword drawn in daylight. In Scorpio, it is the same blade kept in a drawer. Your Moon is in fall, which asks that strength be earned through humility. It feels totally or not at all, and trusts slowly.","Nerve you can lean on. You face what other people flinch from: the diagnosis, the confession, the room after the bad news. You act quickly and are hard to rattle, loyal long after loyalty stops being convenient, and you can tell within a minute who is lying and who is only frightened. Crisis suits you, and you are calm in it.","You can forgive a shouting match within the hour and keep a quiet slight for a decade. The Moon tests people instead of asking them, and the open face hides the verdict until it is final. Silence becomes the punishment. Growth is saying the Moon’s sentence at the Aries pace, while it is still small and the person is still within reach."],"aries-scorpio-taurus":["At twenty you cannot see that yet. You look steady and a little immovable, someone who does not discuss things. The Aries Sun gets on with life in plain daylight: it begins, it tries, it forgives quickly. The Scorpio Moon keeps its own counsel, remembers everything and explains nothing. Hurt does not fade in you. It hardens into a very quiet door, and the Taurus calm stands in front of it so well that few people ever suspect there is one.","Mars rules your Sun and is the old ruler of the Scorpio Moon, so the two lights share an engine of heat and nerve, though a quincunx keeps them from understanding each other. The Moon, in fall, learns its strength through humility, and it is hard-won. Taurus Rising stands directly across the wheel from the Moon, an opposition: your calm face and your private depth are two halves of one trust, and each has to earn the other.","Depth and loyalty. You love once and thoroughly, you can keep a confidence for life, and when you finally speak, the room listens. Your calm is not a performance and your nerve is real. In a crisis you are the one who does not flinch and does not leave.","You can take silence for strength and test the people you love by watching whether they notice. The Taurus front keeps everyone comfortable while the Moon keeps score. Growth is opening the vault before what is inside goes cold, and letting someone see it while it is still alive."],"aries-scorpio-gemini":["That is the contradiction people notice and cannot explain. You are fluent, funny, full of stories, and you tell them all. Yet nobody can say what you actually feel, because the Scorpio Moon files it where the Gemini voice does not go. The Aries Sun is direct, and it is the only part of you that says what it wants without a disguise. So you are open and sealed in the same afternoon, and you rarely find that odd.","The Sun and the Rising are sextile, friendly with each other, and both stand a quincunx from the Moon, which sits at the far point. That is a yod by sign: two lights cooperating while a third keeps asking them to adjust. Mars rules your Sun and is the old ruler of the Moon. The Moon is in fall, so strength has to be built through humility, and the quick talker in front has to learn to hold still when something matters.","Depth with wit. You read people fast and deeply, you keep secrets, and you can deliver a hard truth in a line that makes the whole room laugh and think. You are loyal beyond what you say, and you remember who was kind.","Words become a screen. You may test people with a clever remark and watch what they do with it, then decide in private. The Moon takes offence quietly and holds it. Growth is saying one real sentence, slowly, to someone who has earned it."],"aries-scorpio-cancer":["The body tells it before you do. You fold your arms around your middle, your jaw sets, and your gaze goes a long way off. People see someone warm and protective, a shelter with a soft voice, and the Cancer Rising works hard to keep it that way. The Scorpio Moon feels totally or not at all, and it keeps the record. The Aries Sun is the part that says the plain thing when the thread finally snaps.","Mars rules your Sun and is the old ruler of the Scorpio Moon, so the two lights share an engine, though a quincunx keeps them from quite understanding each other. The Moon, in fall, learns its strength through humility, and the Cancer Rising trines it: two water signs, one shared language of feeling. That trine gives the inner life a protected harbour. The Rising squares the Sun, so the fire is the one light that keeps getting restrained.","Loyalty with depth. You love with your whole body and you keep every promise, you read people well, and you protect what you love with real force. You can be trusted with anything, and people sense it.","Hurt goes down the well and is kept for years. The Cancer front smiles over it and the Scorpio Moon files it, and the Aries Sun, rarely consulted, acts when the string finally breaks. Growth is saying the hurt aloud to the one who caused it, in the same week."],"aries-scorpio-leo":["Some people keep their scars covered. You have learned to show yours, once, to the right person, and then to use it as a map of where not to go again. People meet the Leo Rising: confident, warm, magnetic. The Scorpio Moon feels totally or not at all, and it remembers every detail, every promise. The Aries Sun is the part that goes forward anyway. What looks like pride is often a long apprenticeship in not being hurt twice.","Mars rules your Sun and is the old ruler of the Scorpio Moon, so the two lights share an engine, though a quincunx keeps them from quite understanding each other. The Moon, in fall, learns its strength through humility. It squares Leo Rising, two fixed signs, each sure that it is right: the Rising wants to be seen and the Moon wants to be safe. The Sun trines the Rising and rules it.","Depth with presence. You hold a room and keep a confidence, you read people accurately and do not exploit it, and your loyalty has the weight of memory behind it. When you speak from experience, people listen.","Pride and privacy can lock together. The Leo front protects the image, the Scorpio Moon keeps the file, and the Aries Sun acts when it can no longer wait. You may test people and then judge the results. Growth is showing someone the scar before the story hardens."],"aries-scorpio-virgo":["The question sits behind every handshake. You are direct, quiet and observant, and you give very little away until you know who will be careful with it. People meet the Virgo Rising: neat, modest, evaluating, and often helpful in ways they notice later. The Scorpio Moon keeps the key on a chain. The Aries Sun is the part that says the plain thing when you finally decide a person has earned it.","A yod by sign: the Moon in Scorpio and the Rising in Virgo are sextile, friendly with each other, and both stand a quincunx from the Aries Sun, which sits at the far point. The Sun is the one that keeps being asked to adjust. Mars rules the Sun and is the old ruler of the Moon. The Moon is in fall, so strength has to be built through humility, and Mercury’s Rising supplies the care.","Depth with discipline. You can keep a confidence for life, notice the detail that matters and act on it. Your loyalty is quiet and absolute. People trust you with the thing they would not tell anyone else, and you handle it exactly as promised.","Trust is a test you run silently. The Virgo front watches, the Scorpio Moon files the result, and the Aries Sun acts on a verdict nobody knew was being reached. Growth is asking the question aloud, kindly, before you answer it for them."],"aries-scorpio-libra":["At fifty you will understand that the smile was never fake and never the whole story. In your twenties you were gracious in the front room while a war drum kept time in the cellar. The Libra Rising greets guests with courtesy, the Scorpio Moon sits in the dark with a long memory, and the Aries Sun reaches for the door handle. You will come to see that the drum was loyalty, grief and plain wanting, and not enmity.","Mars rules the Sun and, traditionally, the Scorpio Moon, so will and need share a ruler even though they stand a quincunx, five signs apart. The Moon is in fall, intense but short of ease, and learns through humility. The Libra Rising opposes the Sun and stands a semi-sextile from the Moon, a neighbour with a blind spot, so the surface keeps misjudging how much goes on behind it.","Depth with manners. You can hold a confidence, a grudge turned to understanding, and a room at once. You see motives and say the true thing gently. People feel safe with you because you are not naive. Your loyalty has the weight of a vow, and your courtesy has real edges.","The Libra front hides the intensity so well that nobody can help with it. The Scorpio Moon files, the Aries Sun acts on the file, and the result looks sudden. You may mistake control for peace. Growth is letting one person see the unpolished reaction, and finding that they stay."],"aries-scorpio-scorpio":["You are direct and secretive at once, and both are true. Ask what you want and you will say so plainly, with the gate open. Ask what you are afraid of and the vault door closes without a sound. The Aries Sun is the gate. The Scorpio Moon and Rising are the vault, a doubled water sign with feeling and manner in the same dark room, and you are never more in control than when you seem to be telling everything.","Moon and Rising share Scorpio, so feeling and manner are one guarded thing, and in the older reckoning Mars rules all three lights. The Moon is in fall, so strength is built through humility and is hard-won. The Sun stands a quincunx from both, five signs away, so the gate has little in common with the vault and keeps being asked to adjust. Decisive on the surface, private and intense beneath.","Directness and depth. You say the clear thing and keep the real thing, you survive what flattens others, and you start over without ceremony. Your loyalty is total and your insight is uncomfortable and accurate. People return to you after the storm because you did not leave.","Two Scorpio lights keep the books, and the Aries Sun does the collecting. A Moon in fall learns to bend slowly, and in the meantime it armours. You may mistake being feared for being safe. Growth is letting the gate show the vault once, to someone who has done nothing to earn it."],"aries-scorpio-sagittarius":["The feeling goes low, into the belly and the hips, and stays there like a stone in a pocket. You can stand at a door, chest lifted, grinning, weight a little back, while the lower half of you holds something dark and settled. People meet the Sagittarius Rising, open and laughing. The Scorpio Moon is the deep well, and the Aries Sun is the forge at first light. At dusk the caravan leaves, and the well goes with it.","The Scorpio Moon is in fall, so strength is built through humility and is hard-won. It shares Mars with the Aries Sun, so will and need have one ruler though they stand a quincunx, five signs apart. The Sagittarius Rising trines the Sun and stands a semi-sextile from the Moon, a neighbour that barely sees it, so the cheerful front rarely perceives how deep the interior runs. Decisive outside, private and intense beneath.","Cheer with depth. You can laugh at the funeral and then stay for the real talk. You see motives and still believe in people. You go far and keep your word, and you tell the truth in a way that makes others braver. Your loyalty has the weight of a vow.","The bright front hides the well so well that nobody thinks to ask. You may joke past a wound and carry it for years. The Aries Sun acts on what the Moon files, and the result looks sudden. Growth is letting the laugh stop for a minute, and the well show."],"aries-scorpio-capricorn":["Cathedrals take a century to build, and many have burned and been rebuilt in the same stone, a little lower and a little stronger. That is how you handle a loss. The Capricorn Rising is the stone, composed and unhurried. The Scorpio Moon is what happened in the fire, the phoenix, private and total. The Aries Sun is the war drum that starts the rebuilding the next morning, before anyone has asked.","The Scorpio Moon is in fall, so strength is built through humility and is hard-won. It shares Mars with the Aries Sun, though they stand a quincunx, five signs apart, and it sextiles the Capricorn Rising, water and earth, so interior and front support each other quietly. The Sun squares the Rising, cardinal against cardinal. Decisive outside, private and emotionally intense beneath.","Resilience with weight. You survive what flattens others, rebuild without ceremony and keep what you learn. You are loyal, exact and hard to deceive, you work through grief rather than around it, and you hold others up in a crisis. Your composure has been earned.","The composed front and the intense Moon protect each other so well that nobody helps. You may rebuild alone and confuse endurance with health. The Aries Sun acts on what the Moon files. Growth is letting somebody carry the stone for a day."],"aries-scorpio-aquarius":["Who can I tell the real thing to, and how will I know before I have told them? You ask yourself this in the quiet, with a sealed letter on the desk. The Aquarius Rising is the signal tower: friendly, original, easy to talk to about anything except yourself. The Scorpio Moon is the sealed room beneath it, deep and private. The Aries Sun is the ram on the high ledge who, now and then, sends the letter without warning.","The Scorpio Moon is in fall, so strength is built through humility and is hard-won, and it shares Mars with the Aries Sun, though they stand a quincunx. It squares the Aquarius Rising, fixed against fixed, so intensity and detachment both refuse to move. The Sun sextiles the Rising. Decisive on the surface, private and emotionally intense beneath, and very effectively disguised.","Depth with reach. You read people accurately, keep real secrets and say true things at the right time. You are original, loyal and unflinching. You can stand beside someone in the worst of it without a single platitude, and then help them build something new.","Two fixed lights in a square keep both doors shut, one with a smile and one with a lock. You may share ideas freely and feelings never. The Aries Sun sends the letter at the wrong hour. Growth is telling one friend the true thing slowly, in small instalments."],"aries-scorpio-pisces":["At fifty you will understand that the bell under water was ringing the whole time. In your twenties the Scorpio Moon felt like an eclipse, a private darkness you managed with force. The Pisces Rising was the surface, soft and kind and easy to read wrongly. The Aries Sun was the red thread you followed out of every room. You will hear the bell and see that it was never a threat. It was the part of you that remembered.","Two lights in water and one in fire. The Scorpio Moon is in fall, so strength is built through humility and is hard-won, and it shares Mars with the Aries Sun, though they stand a quincunx. It trines the Pisces Rising, water to water, so interior and front are fluent and nearly indistinguishable. The Sun is a semi-sextile from the Rising. Decisive on the surface, private and intense beneath.","Depth you can trust. You feel at the bottom of things and speak softly about them. You are loyal, perceptive and unafraid of the dark, you forgive slowly and thoroughly, and you stay for the worst of it. Your gentleness is the last thing people expect and the first they remember.","Two water lights flood together, and the Aries Sun answers with force. You may hold a feeling underwater until it surfaces as a decision. Grief and anger share one bell. Growth is letting the bell be heard by one trusted friend before it rings itself."],"aries-sagittarius-aries":["The Sun is at the forge door shouting that it is time. The Rising is already on the step with its boots laced, telling everyone to hurry. The Moon is in the yard saddling something, asking where exactly we are going and whether it is far enough. The world meets the one on the step: cheerful, forthright, headed somewhere. What drives it all is a conviction that tomorrow will be better than today and that the road is where you find out why.","All three lights are fire and the Moon trines the pair, so what you feel, what you intend and what you show point the same way, which is forward. That is the ease, and also the trap: no one inside is ever the dissenting vote. The Aries lights want the first step. The Sagittarius Moon wants the horizon, the meaning of the whole trip, and open air to feel anything at all. They rarely fight. They simply leave together. Your task is to want a destination as well as a direction.","Contagious faith. You walk into a stalled situation and make leaving it seem not only possible but fun. You say the true thing with good humour, and you recover from a setback faster than most people can finish describing it. People borrow your belief that it can work out, and many of them act on it because you were willing to go first.","The Moon needs the door ajar and the Rising is already through it, so you can promise more than you finish and treat a horizon as an answer. Honesty turns careless: the joke or the truth thrown from a moving vehicle, landing on someone who needed you to stay. Growth is the second week, staying for what is no longer new and finishing one road before blessing the next."],"aries-sagittarius-taurus":["There is a leaving in it and a staying. People see the Taurus presence: unhurried, well fed, glad of a good chair and a good story. The Aries Sun and the Sagittarius Moon are both fire, and both would like to be on the road by morning. But you do not leave without provisions, a decent pair of boots and a friend who knows when to expect you. That is why you tend to arrive.","The Sagittarius Moon trines your Sun, so fire talks easily to fire, and appetite for adventure pulls the same way as willingness to act. Taurus Rising stands at an awkward angle to the Moon, a quincunx, with nothing in common. Venus rules it, and it wants a home, a table and something worth defending. The Moon wants the door ajar. You are most yourself when the road is an appetite and home is where you return.","Enthusiasm with a plan. You inspire others to go, and you remember the food, the maps and the people who stayed behind. You are generous, optimistic and hard to discourage, and your good sense turns other people’s grand ideas into something that can actually be eaten.","Two fire lights promise a great deal, and the Taurus side wants it done at a comfortable pace, so you can overcommit and then dig in against the very thing you offered. Restlessness may arrive as a sudden wish to move house. Growth is finishing the journey you are on before you plan the next."],"aries-sagittarius-gemini":["People watch you move between subjects, books, plans and cities and decide you cannot settle. It is a common misreading. You are relentless about a few big questions, and the chatter is how you look for the answers. The Aries Sun starts, the Sagittarius Moon believes in tomorrow, and the Gemini Rising asks everyone you meet what they know. You are easy to underestimate, because the questions are cheerful and the stubbornness is not.","Your Sun trines the Moon, fire to fire, so will and appetite pull in one direction. Sagittarius and Gemini face each other across the wheel, an opposition: the Moon wants the big meaning, and the Rising wants the next fact. Mercury and the Moon disagree about scale, and you spend your life moving between the two. The sextile from Sun to Rising helps. Between them, you are never bored and rarely stuck.","Curiosity with courage. You can start on any subject, meet any stranger, and find a way through any unfamiliar place. You are cheerful in defeat, quick to forgive, and an excellent teacher of the thing you have just learned.","Breadth can become a way of never staying long enough to be changed. The Moon promises the horizon and the Rising offers an easy exit, so a commitment may feel like a cage. Growth is picking one question and giving it a year."],"aries-sagittarius-cancer":["It is Sunday evening, the bag is packed, and you are reassuring someone that you will call. People see the Cancer Rising, a warm, tender, protective presence, someone who would not dream of leaving. The Aries Sun and Sagittarius Moon are both fire, and both are halfway down the road. You go, you do come back, and you bring gifts. Every departure carries a small grief and every arrival a large one.","Sun and Moon trine, fire to fire, so will and appetite pull the same way and you rarely doubt what you want. The Cancer Rising squares the Sun and sits at an awkward angle to the Moon, a quincunx with nothing in common. The Rising wants a home and a safe harbour, the Moon wants the horizon, and Cancer is ruled by the Moon, so the longing for home has a pulse of its own. You live on the line between leaving and returning.","Courage with care. You go farther than most and look after the people you leave behind. You bring back stories, food and good news, you make a stranger’s house feel like yours, and you make your own house a place travellers want to return to.","The two fire lights promise the road, and the Cancer front wants everyone safe, so you can feel guilty for leaving and restless for staying. You may stay too long to avoid the goodbye, then go suddenly. Growth is going gladly, and telling the people you love when you will be back."],"aries-sagittarius-leo":["It is a habit your friends know: you meet trouble with a laugh, take a breath, and then walk straight at it. People meet the Leo Rising, warm, big-hearted, a presence that fills a doorway. The Sagittarius Moon believes tomorrow will be better and says so. The Aries Sun starts the work that makes it true. Nothing about you is hidden or sly, and the simplicity is the gift. You are easy to love and hard to discourage.","A grand trine by sign: Aries, Leo and Sagittarius, all fire, each trine to the other two, a closed circle of ease. Mars rules the Sun, the Sun rules Leo, and Jupiter’s sign carries the Moon. Nothing in the chart resists. The result is confidence, momentum and a long run of luck that can feel like a right. The circle is warm and closed, so what it lacks is an outside view.","Courage with joy. You bring optimism that gets up and does something, you inspire people to try, and you are generous with credit and cheer. You are good at starting, good at celebrating, and good at forgiving.","A closed circle of ease can leave you without a friction that teaches. You may promise more than you can deliver and be sincere about it, then take a correction as an attack. Growth is seeking out one person who disagrees with you, and listening to the end."],"aries-sagittarius-virgo":["The Aries voice is at the door with a war drum, already going. The Sagittarius voice is by the campfire, telling the next story and believing it. The Virgo voice is quietly folding the handkerchief and counting the matches. People meet that last one first: neat, observant, a little modest. They learn later that you are also the one who will take the long road and have a sandwich for it. You live in three registers and mostly agree.","Your Sun trines the Sagittarius Moon, fire to fire, so will and appetite pull the same way. Virgo Rising stands a quincunx from the Sun and square to the Moon, so the careful front has little in common with the first and argues with the second. Mercury rules it, and its job is to edit the dream without killing it. Between them you go far, and arrive prepared.","Adventure with a checklist. You go further than most and come back with the story, the receipt and the map. You make a journey seem possible to people who thought they could not, and you handle the small things that make a big one work.","The Virgo front fights the Moon’s wide horizon with a list, and the Aries Sun acts before either wins. You may promise the whole world and then fuss about the details of getting there. Growth is leaving one thing unplanned, and trusting the road."],"aries-sagittarius-libra":["You are seen at the door of someone else’s party, bottle in one hand, already asking the guest by the coats where they travelled this year, one foot angled back toward the street in case something more interesting happens. The Libra Rising is the generous handshake. The Sagittarius Moon is the appetite for the next place and the bigger story. The Aries Sun is the ram on the high ledge, glancing at the view.","Fire trines fire: the Sun trines the Sagittarius Moon, so want and need run the same way, and the Moon sextiles the Rising, so appetite and manners cooperate. Only the Sun opposes the Rising, so charm and drive take turns on the seesaw, with an arrow on one side and two chairs facing on the other. People want you to stay, and you want to see what is next.","Enthusiasm that includes people. You bring others along, introduce friends who become friends, and treat a trip, a plan or a conversation as a shared adventure. Your honesty is warm and your optimism is catching. You make a hard thing sound like a good invitation.","The restless pair keeps the gracious front permanently open to the next thing, and commitments suffer politely. You can promise warmly and quietly drift. Fairness becomes a way to avoid choosing one chair. Growth is sitting down in one of the two chairs and staying until the conversation ends."],"aries-sagittarius-scorpio":["People take you for the intense one, and the Scorpio Rising earns that: the steady gaze, the stillness, the way you listen as though taking notes for later. They are wrong about the weather. Behind it the Sagittarius Moon is cheerful, curious and happiest with salt wind and a ship’s ticket, and the Aries Sun is lighting the forge for the next trip. Once you trust them, the laugh arrives, big and unguarded, and surprises everyone.","Fire trines fire: the Sun trines the Sagittarius Moon, so want and need pull in the same direction, and Mars rules the Sun while Jupiter rules the Moon, so appetite is large and generous. The Scorpio Rising is the odd sign out, a quincunx from the Sun and a neighbour of the Moon, a semi-sextile that barely sees it. The front is quiet and the interior is a bonfire.","Adventure with depth. You go further than most and come back with a better story and a truer sense of people. You are loyal, funny and fearless, you tell the truth in a way that cheers others, and you choose your friends with real discernment.","Scorpio’s guard and Sagittarius’s wanderlust agree on one thing: do not be pinned down. You may travel in order not to be read, and tell the funny story instead of the true one. The Aries Sun leaves when cornered. Growth is staying on the dock, once, for someone who would be sad to see you go."],"aries-sagittarius-sagittarius":["Five in the morning on the day of a journey is your best hour. The bag is by the door, the road is empty, and all three lights agree: go. The Sagittarius Moon and Rising are the compass needle swinging toward whatever is new, and the Aries Sun is the ram on the high ledge, glancing out. People meet someone cheerful, curious and light on their feet. What they do not see is how long it takes you to be content in one place.","Moon and Rising share Sagittarius, so feeling and manner are one bright animal ruled by Jupiter, and the Aries Sun trines both. It is a doubled fire sign with a third fire sign in support, with almost no friction anywhere. The weakness is the same as the strength: the chart’s only brake is whatever life hands it, and life tends to hand it late.","Optimism that moves. You begin, you welcome, you believe in the next place and the next person, and others catch the belief. You are honest, generous and hard to discourage. You make a journey, a plan or a Monday feel like an invitation.","Three fire lights, no ballast. You may leave before you have finished and promise a return you have not planned. Commitment can feel like a locked door, and you keep testing the handle. Growth is staying one more week than you wanted, and noticing what arrives."],"aries-sagittarius-capricorn":["You plan the trip to the hour, book the table, print the maps, and then you are happiest in the one hour the plan did not cover, around a winter fire with someone who knows a better route. When you are cornered you make a list. When you are tired you make a longer list. When you are delighted you leave a margin on the map and tell nobody it is there. The Capricorn Rising is the plan, and the Sagittarius Moon is the margin.","Fire trines fire: the Sun trines the Sagittarius Moon, so want and need pull the same way. The Capricorn Rising squares the Sun, cardinal against cardinal, and stands a semi-sextile from the Moon, a neighbour with a blind spot, so the serious front rarely sees how much appetite for the horizon lives behind it. Saturn rules the Rising and Jupiter the Moon. Amplified passion and drive.","Adventure with a spine. You travel far, arrive on time and bring everyone home. Your optimism is real and so is your planning, and you can turn a wild idea into an expedition. People rely on your composure and borrow your enthusiasm.","The Capricorn Rising supervises the Moon’s freedom, and the Aries Sun acts before either has finished. You may turn every adventure into a project and every project into a duty. Growth is leaving one weekend with no map, no purpose and no excuse."],"aries-sagittarius-aquarius":["Three voices live in your house. The Aries Sun makes the first stroke of the brush, today, with no sketch. The Sagittarius Moon is the compass needle, always pointing at some place you have not been. The Aquarius Rising hears distant applause from a better future and describes it to everyone as if it were already scheduled. People call you hopeful and mean it as praise, and a little bit as a worry.","An arc of ease: the Sun trines the Sagittarius Moon, and both sextile the Aquarius Rising, so all three lights cooperate and no hard angle disturbs the chart. Fire and air feed one another. Amplified passion, confidence and drive, in a very friendly package. It runs smoothly and quickly, little in it is resisted, and the Sagittarius Moon’s appetite for distance is matched by the Rising’s appetite for the future.","Hope that builds. You believe in the better version of a place or a friend, and you start the work. You are friendly, brave and inventive, you travel in ideas as well as countries, and you bring people along. Your optimism has a plan in it, not just a feeling.","With no hard angle there is no pressure to examine the dream, so you may stay in the future and neglect Tuesday. The easy chart gives easy promises. Growth is finishing a small dull task that nobody will applaud, and noticing that you are still hopeful afterwards."],"aries-sagittarius-pisces":["You are seen at the door with a bag on one shoulder and a lantern in your hand, going out into the rain, a red thread of an idea pulling you along, the compass needle trembling. Later you are seen at the same door, wet through, telling someone that it is all right and the road is there. The Pisces Rising makes you gentle and faraway, the Sagittarius Moon makes you hopeful, and the Aries Sun is the one who actually goes.","Fire trines fire: the Sun trines the Sagittarius Moon, so want and need pull together. Moon and Rising share Jupiter, so faith and appetite run in one stream, though they stand in a square, mutable against mutable, so the interior and the front argue about direction. The Sun is a semi-sextile from the Rising. Amplified passion and drive, with a soft, faraway front.","Faith with legs. You believe in the road and you walk it, and you carry a light for those who have no lantern. You are generous, adventurous and tender, and you make the unknown seem kind. People follow you because you come back.","Jupiter rules two of your lights and inflates both. You may believe the hopeful story you tell, promise the road and mislay the map. The Pisces Rising drifts while the Aries Sun leaps. Growth is checking the weather and the map before the leap, once."],"aries-capricorn-aries":["At fifty you will see what is hard to see at twenty: the hurry was never about speed. It was about being taken seriously, and making something solid enough that nobody could dismiss you. For now people meet a brisk, capable, slightly severe presence with a plan and a first move, who will not wait for a committee. What they miss is the Capricorn Moon, which manages feeling like a task: late, privately, dryly, and with generous provision. Your care looks like competence. It is care all the same.","Capricorn squares Aries, and with all three lights cardinal, nobody in this chart is a follower. The Aries Sun, exalted, wants to start something this week. The Capricorn Moon, in detriment, is at ease with structure, rank and a long season of proof, and has to be taught what it feels. The two pulls are not opposites but cousins, both ambitious, both impatient, running on different clocks. When the Moon sets the plan and the Sun supplies the nerve, little stops you. When they argue, it comes out as overwork.","Initiative that lasts. You can begin and also plan, which is rare, and you carry a project through winter without losing the thrill of its first week. You are reliable under pressure, honest about what something will cost, and good at handing others a clear next step. People feel safer inside your plans than inside most promises.","You can use ambition to avoid asking for anything. Feelings are handled like tasks, scheduled for after the deadline, and rest is earned by collapse rather than by choice. The Moon’s dryness may be mistaken for coldness by the people who most want a softer sentence. Growth is letting someone see the unfinished version of you, and sitting down before the work is done."],"aries-capricorn-taurus":["At nine in the morning you want it done by ten. At nine at night you will wait on the same task for a week without comment. People see the Taurus calm and the Capricorn gravity and conclude you were born old. The Aries Sun knows otherwise: it is fast, it is brave, and it has simply learned to hide the speed inside a plan. You are the one who looks as if you have been climbing for years, and who is still, privately, a sprinter.","The Capricorn Moon squares your Sun, cardinal against cardinal, so what you need and what you want keep trying to lead. The Moon sits in detriment here, working against the grain, which means feeling must be learned and managed rather than simply trusted. Taurus Rising trines the Moon, both earth, so your surface and your private weather agree on stability, and the quiet strength of that pairing carries the Sun through.","Endurance with ignition. You can start a thing fast and keep it going for years, and you can be counted on in every season. Your word is good, your effort shows up as work, and your tenderness arrives as provision.","Feelings go into a ledger and rest becomes a reward you have not earned. The Moon manages emotion like a task, the Rising looks fine, and the Sun burns off the rest in work. Growth is letting someone see you tired, and accepting help without paying it back at once."],"aries-capricorn-gemini":["You carry it in the hands and the jaw. The shoulders lift a little, you start fixing something, and the talk gets faster and lighter, which is exactly when you are feeling the most. People see a quick, funny, capable person, and they do not see the Capricorn Moon at work, managing the feeling like a project. The Aries Sun supplies the nerve and the pace. The result is someone who looks easy and is, privately, carrying a great deal.","The Moon sits in detriment in Capricorn, working against the grain, so you learn to feel by practice and rarely by instinct. It squares your Aries Sun, cardinal against cardinal, and both want to lead. Gemini Rising sextiles the Sun, and a quincunx stands between it and the Moon, so the quick surface and the serious interior have to keep adjusting. A scaffold, not a wall: the structure holds while the work goes on.","Discipline with flair. You can build, plan and joke in the same hour, you deliver on what you promise, and you are calm in a crisis because you have already thought it through. Your tenderness is shown in what you provide, and it lasts.","Feeling gets managed, joked about, scheduled. The Gemini front makes it easy to sound fine, and the Capricorn Moon agrees to the show. Rest is postponed. Growth is stopping mid-task, letting the shoulders drop, and saying aloud what you would otherwise handle alone."],"aries-capricorn-cancer":["Picture a stone house on a ledge, with one lamp lit in the highest window. That is someone who is working hard and caring harder. People meet the Cancer Rising: soft, watchful, a little shy, sincerely warm. The Capricorn Moon manages the feelings like a task, privately and with a straight back. The Aries Sun is the climber who built the house in the first place, and who will not admit that it is lonely.","A T-square by sign: the Moon in Capricorn opposes the Cancer Rising, and the Aries Sun squares both. All three lights are cardinal, and each wants to lead. The Moon sits in detriment, working against the grain, so feeling is learned rather than trusted. The pull between home and duty, between warmth and standing, is the pressure that shapes you. The Sun is at the corner, and the Sun is the one that has to act.","Strength with a soft centre. You provide, protect and persist, and you do it quietly, over years. People lean on you, and you are rarely the one who collapses. Your tenderness takes the form of shelter, and it lasts.","Under so much pressure you may mistake being needed for being loved, and carry the whole house alone. The Capricorn Moon says it is fine, the Cancer front agrees, and the Aries Sun pushes harder. Growth is asking for help while the lamp is still lit, before the oil runs low."],"aries-capricorn-leo":["The question runs under every success. You work hard, you climb, you do it well, and a small voice asks whether it was enough and whether it was seen. People meet the Leo Rising: warm, confident, dressed for the occasion. The Capricorn Moon manages the feelings like a task, privately, with a straight back. The Aries Sun is the one who started climbing before anyone told you to. The warmth is real. So is the loneliness at the top.","The Capricorn Moon sits in detriment and squares your Aries Sun, cardinal against cardinal: what you need and what you want both want to lead. The Sun trines Leo Rising, so the public face supports the Sun, and a quincunx between the Moon and the Rising leaves the interior and the presentation without much in common. The Sun rules Leo. Duty and display keep adjusting to each other.","Ambition with warmth. You lead by example, you finish what you commit to, and your generosity arrives in practical form: a job, an introduction, a fixed roof. People trust you because you have been seen to earn it.","The Capricorn Moon holds feeling to a standard and the Leo front performs the success. You may postpone joy until the work is done, then find the work is never done. Growth is celebrating something small, in company, before it has been earned."],"aries-capricorn-virgo":["At twenty you cannot see that. You are up in the cold morning air, the desk is clear, and you are already working, because that is how you stay calm. People meet the Virgo Rising, neat, reliable, modest, a person who simply gets on with it. The Capricorn Moon manages the feelings like a task. The Aries Sun is the climber who started early and does not talk about it. You will learn, slowly, that you were allowed to stop.","The Capricorn Moon sits in detriment, working against the grain, and squares your Aries Sun, cardinal against cardinal. It trines Virgo Rising, both earth, so the surface and the interior agree about order and effort. The Sun stands a quincunx from the Rising. Two earth lights give you structure and endurance, and the fire supplies the nerve. The cost is that the Sun is rarely allowed to play.","Endurance with ignition. You begin early, work steadily and finish what you said you would. Your standards are high and your word is good, and your tenderness arrives as help done properly. Others rest because you do not.","The Moon manages emotion like a task, the Rising criticises the result, and the Sun pushes harder. You may mistake exhaustion for virtue. Rest becomes a reward you have not yet earned. Growth is stopping at four in the afternoon, once a week, with the list unfinished."],"aries-capricorn-libra":["You are the easiest person at the table to talk to and the hardest on yourself afterwards, and both are true. The Libra Rising is lovely company, attentive, well turned out, interested in you. The Capricorn Moon keeps the books, and at twilight it stands on the balcony going over what you said, how it landed and what it will cost. The Aries Sun is the ram on the high ledge, who would rather climb than discuss.","A T-square by sign: Sun and Rising oppose, and the Capricorn Moon squares both. Every corner is cardinal, so every corner wants to lead. The Moon is in detriment, so feeling arrives the hard way, as duty, standards and a long view. Venus rules the Rising and Saturn the Moon, so you are charming and serious in equal measure, and the Sun is pressed to push on both. The tension builds ambition.","Charm with a spine and a plan. You begin early, hold standards and make others feel looked after while you work. You win trust slowly and keep it. Your manners are real, your word is good and your ambition has taste. People follow you up the hill because the company is good.","The Capricorn Moon treats feeling as weakness, the Libra front covers it, and the Aries Sun works harder to compensate. You may be pleasant all day and bleak at night, with nobody told. Rest feels like an unearned luxury. Growth is naming one need to one friend at dusk, before it becomes a duty."],"aries-capricorn-scorpio":["The feeling goes to the jaw and the upper back. You stand very straight, hands in pockets, weight even, face composed, and you wait. Nobody can tell whether you are calm or furious, and often you cannot either. The Scorpio Rising is the steady gaze. The Capricorn Moon manages the rest like a project. The Aries Sun is the part that, at some point, leaves the gate unlatched and walks through before anyone has seen you decide.","Sun and Moon square each other, cardinal against cardinal, so what you do and what you need collide and sharpen. The Moon is in detriment, so feeling has to be learned, as duty and long effort. The Capricorn Moon sextiles the Scorpio Rising, earth and water supporting each other, so interior and front cooperate quietly. Mars rules the Sun and, traditionally, the Rising. Bold outside, patient and cautious underneath.","Strength that lasts. You can endure more than most, plan further and act without drama. Your word is binding, your loyalty is steady, and your self-command is a gift to people who cannot manage theirs. You are the one still standing, and still kind, at the end of a long winter.","Two guarded lights and one fast fire. You may hold a feeling for years because showing it would be a breach, and the Aries Sun will occasionally breach it for you. Rest and tenderness look like weakness. Growth is letting the jaw unclench in company, and calling that a skill."],"aries-capricorn-sagittarius":["Picture a clock tower standing at the edge of a map whose borders have not been drawn. The tower keeps exact time, and the roads beyond it go on past the margin. That is how you are built. The Capricorn Moon is the clock, serious about duty and long effort. The Sagittarius Rising is the road, laughing and open. The Aries Sun is the spearpoint at the front, first to step off the edge with a schedule in the other hand.","The Capricorn Moon is in detriment, working against the grain, so feeling is learned the hard way, as duty and standards. It squares the Aries Sun, cardinal against cardinal, and stands a semi-sextile from the Sagittarius Rising, a neighbour that barely sees it. The Sun trines the Rising. Saturn rules the Moon and Jupiter the Rising, so discipline and expansion share one chart. Bold outside, patient and cautious underneath.","Adventure with a plan and a clock. You travel far and arrive on time, start boldly and finish properly, and your optimism has a budget. You are generous within your means and honest about them. People trust you to lead the long expedition.","The Capricorn Moon treats feeling as duty, the Sagittarius Rising treats duty as an obstacle, and the Aries Sun does both at speed. You may overwork to earn a holiday you then cannot enjoy. Pleasure feels like something to be earned. Growth is taking the road for no reason, one afternoon, without the schedule."],"aries-capricorn-capricorn":["Have I earned this yet? That question sits under almost everything you want: the raise, the rest, the affection. You ask it in a very steady voice. The Capricorn Moon and Rising are the slate, cold, composed and old for their years, and they set the terms. The Aries Sun is the torch inside it, the spearpoint that wants to go now and burns hot, a winter fire in a stone room whose warmth people feel before they see it.","Moon and Rising share Capricorn, so feeling and manner are one serious animal ruled by Saturn, and the Aries Sun squares both, cardinal against cardinal. The Moon is in detriment, working against the grain, so need arrives as duty and has to be learned as tenderness. Bold outside, patient and cautious underneath, with the fire as the sole dissenter, outvoted every day.","Strength that ages well. You begin early, bear weight and finish what others abandon. You are dry, funny, loyal and exact. People feel steadier near you, and are surprised by the fire when you finally let it show.","Two Capricorn lights treat desire as a debt and rest as a reward you have not yet paid for. The Aries Sun pushes harder to prove it. You may be a monument at forty and a stranger to your own wants. Growth is wanting something small and obvious, and having it before you earn it."],"aries-capricorn-aquarius":["At fifty you will understand that the cold years were saving up water. In your twenties the Capricorn Moon felt like a frozen river: duty, standards, a stiff upper lip over everything. The Aquarius Rising looked cool and friendly from a distance, the Aries Sun looked ready to run, and under the river ice the jar was filling. You will see the thaw come in your forties and understand that the long discipline gave the water somewhere to go.","The Capricorn Moon is in detriment, working against the grain, so feeling is learned the hard way, as duty. It squares the Aries Sun, cardinal against cardinal, and the Sun sextiles the Aquarius Rising. Saturn rules the Moon and, traditionally, the Rising, so interior and front share a planet while standing a semi-sextile, neighbours that barely see each other. Bold outside, patient and cautious underneath.","Discipline with imagination. You plan long, build slowly and take real risks for ideas you believe in. You are dry, loyal and original, you improve with age, and you teach younger people to wait without despair. Your steadiness is the other half of your daring.","Saturn guards both Moon and Rising, so the interior is cold and the front is cool, and the Aries Sun alone supplies the heat. You may postpone joy for decades, with a good reason. Growth is letting the thaw begin early, with one pleasure you did not earn."],"aries-capricorn-pisces":["You are the gentlest-looking climber on the mountain and the one doing the hardest work, and both are true. The Pisces Rising is soft, receptive, a little faraway, as though a hymn were being heard through a wall. The Capricorn Moon is the quarry underneath, stone, duty and a very long ascent. The Aries Sun makes the first stroke of the brush, the first step off the ledge. People see the softness, and then discover that the stone is humming with something very tender.","The Capricorn Moon is in detriment, working against the grain, so feeling is learned the hard way, as duty. It squares the Aries Sun, cardinal against cardinal, and sextiles the Pisces Rising, earth and water supporting each other, so interior and front quietly cooperate. The Sun is a semi-sextile from the Rising. Bold outside, patient and cautious underneath, with the softest face of the three at the front.","Tenderness with endurance. You carry a great deal for a long time and do it gently. You are imaginative, dependable and brave, and you build things that shelter people. Your discipline is an act of love, and others can tell.","The Capricorn Moon treats softness as an indulgence, the Pisces Rising cannot help it, and the Aries Sun pushes on. You may hide your tenderness from yourself under a schedule. Growth is letting the hymn be heard, out loud, on the way up."],"aries-aquarius-aries":["At the door of the party you announce yourself with something half joke and half dare, and within ten minutes you are deep in talk with the one guest who disagrees with everyone. You say startling, honest things about the host’s plan, the group’s assumption, the quietly absurd rule that everyone follows. Your friends are many and varied. Your close friends are few, and you guard their independence like your own. Around midnight you are texting from the car, coat already on, which is how the evening ends: warmly, and without a goodbye.","Aquarius sits a sextile from the Aries Sun and Rising, air with fire, so the cooperation is real once it is used. Aries wants to do something now. The Aquarius Moon wants to know whether it is the right thing, and whether anyone’s freedom is being quietly taken. It is fixed, so opinions set hard and feelings are handled at a distance, through ideas. The Aries lights are direct in a way the Moon admires in theory and fears in practice. You are at your best when the Moon names the cause and the others spend their speed on it.","Courage with a cause. You say the unpopular thing first and mean it, you recruit allies by being truly interested in them, and you are not frightened by disapproval or by novelty. Friends find you loyal and very easy to talk to, because you never ask them to be someone they are not. Ideas leave your head and enter the world.","The Moon files feeling under theory, so you can announce that you are fine in a perfectly pleasant voice while you plainly are not. Independence becomes armour, and closeness is read as capture, so you leave a room just before it would have held you. Growth is staying ten minutes past the point where intimacy begins, and saying one need in plain words."],"aries-aquarius-taurus":["You sit with the room, nod at the plan and seem content, and people go away believing you are as settled as you look. In fact the Aries Sun has already decided and the Aquarius Moon is thinking about something entirely different, with the window open. You are more independent than your manner suggests, more curious about strangers, and far less attached to the usual way than your chair implies. The surprise, when it comes, is that you had a view all along.","The Aquarius Moon sextiles your Sun, an easy angle: independence and initiative support each other, and you rarely feel pulled between wanting and being. The tension is with Taurus Rising, which squares the Moon, two fixed signs each sure it is right. The Rising wants routine, comfort and a known way home. The Moon wants room to be strange and a friend who does not ask why. Venus rules the face you wear, and the face is warmer than the mind.","A settled manner around original thinking. You can propose something odd and have it received, because you sound so steady. You make friends across every difference, hold a position under pressure, and bring a fresh idea to the table without upsetting the table.","Detachment can pass for calm. You may withdraw into your own ideas when closeness gets heavy, and the Taurus front means nobody notices you have gone. Two fixed lights turn a small disagreement into a standoff. Growth is naming one feeling to one person, in plain words, before you leave."],"aries-aquarius-gemini":["Everyone else’s windows are dark. Yours is lit, because the Aquarius Moon works best when the world has gone quiet, and the Gemini Rising cannot leave a thought unsaid. The Aries Sun wants to do something about it by breakfast. People meet someone quick, friendly, funny, always a little ahead of the conversation. What they do not see is the hour when you are alone with a problem, and happiest.","Two air signs and one fire: the Aquarius Moon sextiles your Sun and trines Gemini Rising, and the Rising sextiles the Sun, an arc of ease where nothing is pulled out of shape. Mars lights the Sun, Mercury lends the Rising its tongue, and the Moon supplies the distance. The risk is a chart so comfortable with ideas that the body gets left outside, and the people in it.","Original thinking with the nerve to try it. You see what is coming, say it clearly, and begin. You make friends across every difference, you carry an easy humour, and you have a talent for making strange ideas feel reasonable.","Distance can pass for calm. You may reach for an idea when what is needed is a hand, and the quick Gemini voice makes the detachment sound like wit. Growth is closing the laptop, stepping outside, and telling one person what you actually feel."],"aries-aquarius-cancer":["It is a habit you notice more than anyone: you stand a little back from the people you care about, close enough to help and far enough to breathe. People see the Cancer Rising, a warm, protective presence, and assume you want to be held. You do, in your way. The Aquarius Moon needs air and friendship, and the Aries Sun needs a cause. The result is someone deeply loyal and slightly unreachable, like a house of glass in the rain.","The Aquarius Moon sextiles your Sun, so independence and initiative help each other. The Cancer Rising squares the Sun and sits a quincunx from the Moon, so the soft, clinging front and the cool, free interior have little in common. Cancer is ruled by the Moon and asks for closeness, and the Moon in Aquarius asks for room. The Sun mediates by doing, and by doing things for people rather than sitting with them.","Loyalty with freedom. You care about people without crowding them, you see what a family or a group needs, and you build it. You can be warm and original at once, and you give people space to be who they are.","Distance can look like coolness, and the Cancer front makes it worse by seeming to want closeness it then withdraws. You may feel deeply and say it only through action. Growth is one sentence a week that says how much someone matters, in words."],"aries-aquarius-leo":["The Leo one stands in the light and loves it. The Aquarius one stands at the back, watching how the room works, and has questions. The Aries one is already at the gate, ready to go and start something. People meet the Leo Rising: warm, charismatic, generous with attention. They do not always meet the Aquarius Moon, which prefers a friend to a fan. You want to be seen, and you want to be free, and you have learned not to ask which matters more.","The Aquarius Moon sextiles your Sun, so initiative and independence help each other. It sits directly across the wheel from Leo Rising, an opposition: the audience and the observer, the warm front and the cool inner. The Sun trines the Rising and rules it. When all three cooperate you are a leader who lets the room breathe. When they do not you swing between performing and vanishing.","Warmth with freedom. You inspire people without owning them, you bring friends from every circle to one table, and you can lead a crowd and still think for yourself. Your originality and your generosity are the same impulse.","The Leo front wants the room and the Aquarius Moon wants to be left alone, so you may arrive with a bang and disappear with no explanation. Closeness can feel like a demand and applause like a cage. Growth is staying one hour past the point you would normally leave."],"aries-aquarius-virgo":["At six in the morning the desk is clear and you are at the window with a marker, drawing a plan on the glass. People meet the Virgo Rising: neat, observant, modest. They see the care. They do not always see the Aquarius Moon, which wants the plan to be new and the future to be fairer, or the Aries Sun, which wants the first brick laid by lunch. The marker comes off in the end, and the plan is already in your head.","A yod by sign: the Aries Sun and Aquarius Moon are sextile, friendly with each other, and both stand a quincunx from the Virgo Rising, which sits at the far point. So the front keeps being asked to adjust to two lights that cooperate and do not need it. Mercury rules the Rising and does the editing. The chart is quick and original, and its manner is much more careful than its ideas.","Original thinking that gets built. You see how something could be better, draw it clearly, and begin. You are exact, friendly and brave, you make strange ideas look practical, and you can carry a team through the dull middle.","The Virgo front keeps the plan tidy while the Aquarius Moon keeps the people at a distance. You may refine a diagram while a friend waits to be asked. The Aries Sun acts before the checking is done. Growth is showing the draft to one person early, and letting it be messy."],"aries-aquarius-libra":["People think you are the friendliest person they have met, and in a way you are. The Libra Rising makes everyone welcome, and the Aquarius Moon is warm about humanity at large. What they misread is the gate. It is unlatched, not absent. You are free to walk out of any room that asks you to give up a principle, and you will do it politely and without looking back. The Aries Sun is why.","Air carries the chart. The Aquarius Moon trines the Libra Rising, an ease between feeling and manner, and sextiles the Aries Sun, cooperation that works when it is used. The Sun opposes the Rising, the seesaw: charm on one side, independence on the other, and you tend to meet your own boldness in friends. The Moon is detached in the best sense, so loyalty goes to ideas and fairness before moods.","Friendly independence. You include people without owning them, believe in a fairer way of doing things and begin it. You listen, argue kindly and introduce strangers who should know each other. Your courage is cheerful and your manners are a form of respect.","A detached Moon and a sociable front make it easy to be liked and not known. You may serve the group and keep every private need behind the gate. The Aries Sun leaves quickly when cornered, and friends may hear about it afterwards. Growth is staying one more hour in the awkward conversation."],"aries-aquarius-scorpio":["At three in the morning you are most awake. The signal tower is lit: a plan, an idea, a message to someone you have not decided to send. The Aquarius Moon wants the idea to be new and fair and free. The Scorpio Rising keeps the key to the locked door beneath it. The Aries Sun is the spearpoint of the whole thing, wanting to begin by sunrise. By day you look composed and watchful. At night you are making something nobody has seen.","The Sun sextiles the Aquarius Moon, so wanting and needing cooperate when used. The Aquarius Moon squares the Scorpio Rising, fixed against fixed, so detachment and intensity pull against each other: you are reserved because you feel strongly and detached because you are guarded. Mars rules the Sun and, traditionally, the Rising, so will and gaze are kin. Expressive, fast-moving and mentally energised.","Vision with nerve. You see where things are going and you begin, you hold your own counsel and keep your word, and you notice what others hide. You can be fair to strangers and loyal to a few. Your ideas have both an edge and a reason.","Square fixed signs dig in, and detachment and secrecy reinforce each other. You may build a beautiful idea in solitude and resent that nobody came to the tower. The Aries Sun may abandon it on a whim. Growth is sending the signal before it is perfect, to one person who matters."],"aries-aquarius-sagittarius":["You treat every friendship as a door with no handle on the outside. You will open it gladly, widely, with a bottle in your hand, but you want to be the one who decides when, and you do not enjoy being knocked at. When you are cornered you give people space. When you are tired you give them more. When you are delighted you invite a stranger in, then drift off to the next conversation, leaving them warm.","An arc of ease: the Sun sextiles the Aquarius Moon, the Moon sextiles the Sagittarius Rising, and the Sun trines the Rising, so all three lights cooperate and no hard angle sits anywhere in the chart. Aquarius gives the Moon detachment and a taste for ideas, and Sagittarius gives the Rising warmth and range. The risk is the opposite of tension: nothing makes you stay in the difficult conversation.","Friendliness with room in it. You include everyone, push no one, and make strangers feel they belong. You think about the future, argue happily and keep a wide, loyal circle. Your courage is cheerful and your fairness is real.","With every angle in agreement, there is little friction to teach you to stay. You may love people generously and at a safe distance, and call it freedom. Hard conversations can be abandoned for the next idea. Growth is giving one friend the handle on your side of the door."],"aries-aquarius-capricorn":["Three voices live in your house. The Aries Sun is the ram on the high ledge, wanting to go now. The Aquarius Moon is behind a door with no handle on the outside, friendly to everyone and opening for almost no one. The Capricorn Rising stands at the cathedral gate in a good coat, making the whole arrangement look official and reliable. People meet the coat, find the door interesting, and rarely see the ram.","Saturn rules the Capricorn Rising and, traditionally, the Aquarius Moon, so front and interior share a planet and a taste for structure, though they stand a semi-sextile, neighbours who barely see each other. The Sun sextiles the Moon, cooperation that works when used, and squares the Rising, cardinal against cardinal. Expressive, fast-moving and mentally energised, in a very composed frame.","Order with ideas. You make unusual plans credible and keep them on schedule. You think for the long term, argue reasonably and organise people without trampling them. Your courage is quiet and your loyalty is to what is fair. People find you reliable and also unexpectedly original.","The coat and the door both keep people at a distance, so you may be respected more than known. The Aries Sun leaves a room when it is boxed in, and nobody understood that it was boxed in. Growth is leaving the door on the latch for one trusted friend."],"aries-aquarius-aquarius":["You are seen at the open window while the storm comes in, not alarmed, just interested, taking notes. The Aquarius Moon and Rising together make you cool, curious and friendly from a distance, a door with no handle outside. The Aries Sun is the flint and spark behind them, and when something finally strikes you, you act at once, in the first person, and surprise everybody who thought you were only watching.","Moon and Rising share Aquarius, so feeling and manner are one cool, original animal under Saturn and Uranus, and the Aries Sun sextiles both, fire and air in cooperation. A doubled air sign with fire in support. Expressive, fast-moving, mentally energised. The weak point is that nothing in it demands warmth, so warmth has to be chosen on purpose.","Original, brave and friendly. You think ahead, start the thing and include everyone, with real respect for freedom, yours and theirs. You are calm in a storm and clear about what you believe. People feel permitted to be strange near you.","Two Aquarius lights keep a pleasant distance, and the Aries Sun leaps over it only in emergencies. You may be loved by many and known by few, and call that independence. Feelings are analysed rather than felt. Growth is closing the window and staying in the room for one conversation."],"aries-aquarius-pisces":["People think you are vague: a faraway look, an answer that arrives late, a mind that seems to be somewhere over the water. They are misreading the antenna. The Aquarius Moon is tracking a signal tower in the next decade, and the Pisces Rising is the fog around it, soft-focus, kind, receptive. The Aries Sun gets up in the cold morning air and does something about what the signal said, which is why your friends often find that you were right, and early.","Three neighbouring signs run in a row, Aries, Pisces and Aquarius, so the Sun and Rising make a semi-sextile and the Moon and Rising make another: each light barely sees the next, with a blind spot at every join. The Sun sextiles the Aquarius Moon, cooperation that works when it is used. Expressive, fast-moving, mentally energised, behind a soft and receptive front.","Foresight with kindness. You pick up what is coming before others do, say it gently, and then start the work. You are original, brave and easy to talk to, and you are good with people who feel they do not fit. Your oddness reassures other odd people.","Because each light barely sees the next, you may know something and not know how you know it. You may be detached and absorbed in the same minute. The Aries Sun acts before the signal is checked. Growth is writing down what you sense, and testing it against one fact."],"aries-pisces-aries":["You are blunt and porous at once. You will tell someone a difficult truth with your chin up and no cushion, and then carry their wince around until bedtime. People meet the first thing: the brisk, brave, quick-footed person who takes the lead and seems built for impact. What the Moon knows is how much of the room came home with you, whose mood, whose silence. You go from charging to needing a long, quiet hour with water, music or a dark room, and nobody sees the switch.","Pisces sits one sign beyond Aries, a semi-sextile, neighbours who share neither element nor mode and see each other badly. The Aries Sun and Rising decide in a second. The Pisces Moon is mutable water: it absorbs the room, hears what is not said, and needs solitude to learn which feelings are its own. So the fire often acts on a mood that belongs to someone else. Mars is the strike. The Moon is the weather the strike falls into. Let the Moon speak first, even briefly.","Courageous compassion. You cross a street for a stranger, step into someone else’s argument to defend the person who is not there, and do it without a speech. Your intuition is quick enough for the Aries lights to act on, so you are often the first to know someone is struggling and the first to move. The vulnerable feel they have a protector.","Pisces takes in the mood and Aries acts on it, so you may pick a fight over a feeling that began in someone else. You can also vanish into sleep, fantasy or a screen when the room becomes too much, and call it recovering. Growth is asking whose feeling this is before you charge, and keeping a regular hour of water and quiet that you do not have to earn."],"aries-pisces-taurus":["Your hands warm, your breathing slows, and the room seems to lean in. People see an unhurried, grounded person with a lovely, easy presence, and they bring you their troubles. The Pisces Moon takes it all in. The Aries Sun, quietly, wants to act on it, and you have to decide which of the two gets to answer. Most days you do both: you listen, and then you get up and do the practical thing that nobody else thought of.","Pisces, Aries and Taurus run in a row, so every light has a neighbour and the angles are soft. The Pisces Moon sits just behind your Sun, a semi-sextile with a small blind spot: the fire cannot quite see the water. The Moon sextiles Taurus Rising, which helps. Venus lends the soft feelings a body and a routine to live in, and the grounded front keeps the tides from flooding the house.","Compassion that gets up and does something. You feel what others feel, and because of the Aries Sun you move toward it rather than away. People are safe with you, and your steadiness makes you a good place to bring a trouble.","You can take on other people’s weather and mistake it for your own, and the Taurus calm hides how much you are carrying. Sleep, solitude and water are not luxuries for you. Growth is setting a boundary early and gently, before the tide comes in."],"aries-pisces-gemini":["Cold morning air, salt drying on the skin, a head full of radio. That is the feeling of this combination: tingling, a little exposed, wide awake. People see the Gemini quickness, the questions and the quick hands. The Pisces Moon is soaked in everything it has just heard, including what belonged to someone else. The Aries Sun gets up anyway and does the next thing. Talking is how you dry off.","The Pisces Moon sits just behind your Aries Sun, a semi-sextile, with a faint blind spot between them: the fire cannot quite see the water. Pisces and Gemini are square, two mutable signs with different appetites, so what you feel and how you speak keep crossing wires. The Sun sextiles the Rising, a friendly bridge. The fire gets things going, the water tells you what it cost, and the air talks about it afterwards.","Sensitivity that moves. You catch the mood in a room and do something about it, you talk people down, and you can be very funny while meaning every word. Your imagination and your nerve work well together.","Absorbing the room and then narrating it can leave you unsure what is yours. The quick talk covers the tiredness, and the Aries Sun pushes on. Growth is silence, water, an early night, and a boundary set before the evening’s weather arrives."],"aries-pisces-cancer":["You ask it at parties, on trains, in the quiet after an argument, and the honest answer is often both. The Pisces Moon takes in everything, and the Cancer Rising takes in even more, then protects you with a shy, warm, careful manner. People see the soft shell. The Aries Sun is the part that gets up, with real courage, and does something about whatever it was. You hear the hymn through the wall and you go next door to see who is singing.","Pisces and Cancer are both water, and the Moon trines the Rising, so inner life and manner share one language and flow easily. The Sun sits just ahead of the Moon, a semi-sextile with a slight blind spot, and squares the Rising. So the water is fluent and well protected, and the fire is the odd one out, forever being asked to calm down. Cancer is ruled by the Moon, so mood sets the weather.","Sensitivity with courage. You feel what others feel and move toward it, you comfort without being asked, and you protect the vulnerable with real nerve. Your imagination is generous and your instincts are right more often than you think.","Two water lights soak up everything, and the Aries Sun cannot always tell whose weather it is acting on. You may take on a trouble that was not yours and fight for it. Growth is quiet, solitude and one boundary, set early, before you pick up someone else’s feeling."],"aries-pisces-leo":["At twenty it feels like one. The room empties, the music stops, and the Pisces Moon floods with everything it took in during the evening. People meet the Leo Rising, warm, generous, a presence with a little light in it. They do not see the estuary behind it, where the feeling comes in and out with the tide. The Aries Sun is what gets you to the next thing. You will learn that the quiet after the show is where you finally hear what you felt.","The Pisces Moon sits just behind your Aries Sun, a semi-sextile, a blind spot in which the fire cannot quite see the water. It stands a quincunx from Leo Rising, with little in common: the front wants to shine and the Moon wants to dissolve. The Sun trines the Rising and rules it, so the performance follows the Sun even when the Moon is elsewhere.","Warmth with imagination. You feel what the room feels and shape it into something that lifts people, you comfort without being asked, and you give generously from a deep supply. Your sensitivity makes the performance kind.","You may absorb the applause and the room’s mood together and be unable to tell which is yours. The Leo front shows a brave face and the Moon drowns quietly. Growth is solitude, water and an early night after the big evening, with no explanation owed."],"aries-pisces-virgo":["It is a contradiction that nobody around you can quite reconcile. You are neat, modest and exact, the person who labels the spice jars, and you are soaked in feeling, the person who cries at a hymn heard through a wall. When one is under pressure it hides in the other. The Aries Sun gets up and does the next thing, and the next thing is usually practical, which suits the front and rescues the water.","The Pisces Moon and Virgo Rising face each other across the wheel, an opposition: the dream and the checklist, the sea and the jar. Mercury rules the Rising and the Moon dissolves what it sorts, so you rebuild the order daily. The Sun sits a step ahead of the Moon, a semi-sextile with a blind spot, and stands a quincunx from the Rising. The fire is the one that gets things moving.","Sensitivity with method. You feel what others feel and then do something useful about it. You listen well and fix what you hear, you can be tender and exact, and you give care in a form people can actually use. Your imagination is generous.","Every feeling has to be filed, and the Pisces Moon keeps overflowing the files. You may take on other people’s troubles as projects and burn out on the list. Growth is letting a feeling stay unsorted overnight, and an act of kindness stay unlabelled."],"aries-pisces-libra":["The feeling arrives as a hum behind the breastbone and a softness in the feet, as though a tuning fork had been struck somewhere in the house. You carry it in the chest first, then in the soles, which is why you stand a little off balance when someone you love is hurting. People meet the Libra Rising, polished and kind. The Pisces Moon is the lullaby underneath. The Aries Sun opens the gate and walks out to do something about it.","Sun and Moon are neighbours, a semi-sextile with a blind spot: what you do and what you need barely see each other. Pisces and Libra are five signs apart, a quincunx, so the dreaming interior and the gracious front have never properly been introduced. The Sun opposes the Rising, a seesaw. Pisces is where Venus is traditionally exalted, so front and interior share a taste for tenderness.","Tenderness with initiative. You sense what is needed and go and do it, gracefully. Your kindness is practical, your imagination is generous and your charm has real depth. People tell you things they have told no one else, and you act on them quietly.","The Pisces Moon absorbs the weather in the room, the Libra Rising smooths it over, and the Aries Sun runs off to fix it. You may carry other people’s moods as your own and call it tact. Boundaries blur in the name of harmony. Growth is pausing to ask whose feeling it is."],"aries-pisces-scorpio":["Think of the roots under an old house. Nobody sees them, nobody thanks them, and they hold up everything above. That is how the Pisces Moon works: a long, wordless attachment to people and to what cannot be named. The Scorpio Rising is the floorboards, steady and closed. The Aries Sun is the one at the door in the cold morning air, who acts, who says the plain thing, and who has no idea how much of you is under the floor.","Two lights in water and one in fire. The Pisces Moon trines the Scorpio Rising, so feeling and manner are fluent in each other and nearly indistinguishable: others read your depth at once and cannot tell mood from intention. The Sun is a semi-sextile from the Moon, a neighbour with a blind spot, and a quincunx from the Rising, though Mars rules the Sun and, in the old reckoning, the Rising. The fire is the visible part.","Depth that moves. You feel the tide of other people’s lives and know what to do about it, you are intuitive without being passive, and you protect what you love. Your compassion has teeth, and your courage has roots. People feel held by you.","Two water lights soak up every mood, and the Aries Sun answers by leaving or by lunging. You may take on other people’s weather in silence and resent it in the same silence. Boundaries become walls. Growth is saying “this is yours, not mine” aloud."],"aries-pisces-sagittarius":["Is that a sign, or am I only hoping it is? You ask it in the fog, standing at the river with the compass needle trembling, and mostly you decide to go anyway. People meet the Sagittarius Rising, open and bright, the one with news. The Pisces Moon is the river fog, absorbing everything and trusting the feeling it cannot name. The Aries Sun is the flint, wanting to strike a spark now rather than wait for the weather to clear.","Jupiter rules the Sagittarius Rising and, traditionally, the Pisces Moon, so need and manner share a planet, though they stand in a square, mutable against mutable: faith and appetite in the same hands, and often in argument. The Sun trines the Rising, so how you seem and who you are agree, and is a semi-sextile from the Moon, a neighbour with a blind spot. Decisive on the surface, private and intense beneath.","Faith that moves. You trust the unseen enough to start, and your courage is tender. You feel what others feel, tell it as a story that helps, and believe in people before they have earned it. Your imagination is generous and your optimism is catching.","The Pisces Moon absorbs, the Sagittarius Rising inflates, and the Aries Sun acts on both. You may take a mood for a sign and a hope for a plan. Boundaries blur in the name of belief. Growth is waiting for one piece of evidence before the next leap."],"aries-pisces-capricorn":["At fifty you will understand that the sprint at twenty and the mountain path at forty were one journey, and that the lantern in the rain was the tenderness you kept under your coat. The Capricorn Rising wore the coat. The Pisces Moon carried the lantern, feeling everyone’s weather. The Aries Sun kept going. You thought the softness was a weakness to be managed. It was the thing that lit the path, and others followed it.","The Pisces Moon sextiles the Capricorn Rising, water and earth, so interior and front cooperate: the feeling is given form and the form is given feeling. The Sun squares the Rising, cardinal against cardinal, and is a semi-sextile from the Moon, a neighbour with a blind spot. Decisive on the surface, private and intense beneath, and often steadier than you feel.","Tenderness with structure. You feel deeply and act practically, and you carry people through weather and then help them rebuild. You are imaginative and dependable, brave and gentle. Your composure comforts others because it is clearly not coldness.","The Pisces Moon absorbs everything, the Capricorn Rising declines to show it, and the Aries Sun pushes on regardless. You may carry a great deal in silence and call it strength. Exhaustion arrives as a surprise. Growth is saying “I am wet through” before the climb, not at the top."],"aries-pisces-aquarius":["You seem the coolest, calmest company imaginable, and you are absorbing everything: moods, weather, other people’s unspoken sentences. Both are true, and the second is the cause of the first. The Aquarius Rising is the glass house, bright and transparent. The Pisces Moon is the estuary where every river empties. The Aries Sun is the forge at first light, the one hard, clear point that makes decisions. The calm exterior is working very hard to stay calm.","Three neighbouring signs run in a row, Aries, Pisces and Aquarius, so Sun and Moon make a semi-sextile and Moon and Rising make another: each barely sees the next, with a blind spot at every join. The Sun sextiles the Rising, cooperation that works when it is used. Decisive on the surface, private and emotionally intense beneath, with a cool, friendly front on top.","Sensitivity with distance. You feel what others feel and still keep your head, you act kindly and at the right moment, and you see the situation as a whole. Your compassion is practical and your imagination is original. People tell you things, and then feel better.","Because each light barely sees the next, feelings pass down the line without being recognised. You may be overwhelmed and call it a mood, or take on the room’s weather and call it tact. The Aries Sun then acts on a feeling that is not yours. Growth is asking whose weather this is."],"aries-pisces-pisces":["The feeling goes through the whole skin at once: cold feet, wet eyes, a hum in the chest, and a tendency to lean on doorframes. You stand a little slanted, as if listening. The Pisces Moon and Rising are one soft, receptive, shape-shifting presence, a lantern in rain, fog on a river. The Aries Sun is the flint and the spark, the one point of hard clarity in the whole weather, and it keeps striking, even in the fog.","Moon and Rising share Pisces, so feeling and manner are one fluid animal ruled by Jupiter and Neptune, and the Aries Sun is a semi-sextile from both, the neighbouring sign that barely sees them. The fire is the odd one out in its own chart: small, bright and constantly surrounded. Decisive on the surface, private and intense beneath.","Compassion that acts. You feel everything and still begin things, which is rare. Your kindness is immediate, your imagination is large and your spark is reliable. People find a place beside you where they are neither judged nor stalled.","Two water lights flood the single fire, and it may sputter, or flare out of all proportion. You may absorb the day’s weather and spend the evening not knowing which feelings were yours. Boundaries blur. Growth is choosing one thing a day that is clearly yours, and doing it."]});
